E_40_and_higher" title="GNOME">GNOME 48</a></span></div></div></div></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="white-space: nowrap;"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Programmer" title="Programmer">Developer</a></th><td class="infobox-data">Debian Project</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="white-space: nowrap;">OS family</th><td class="infobox-data"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unix-like" title="Unix-like">Unix-like</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="white-space: nowrap;">Working state</th><td class="infobox-data">Current</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="white-space: nowrap;">Source model</th><td class="infobox-data"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Free_software" title="Free software">Free</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="white-space: nowrap;">Initial release</th><td class="infobox-data">16<span typeof="mw:Entity">&nbsp;</span>August 1993<span class="noprint"><span typeof="mw:Entity">;</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>33 years ago</span><span style="display:none"><span typeof="mw:Entity">&nbsp;</span>(<span class="bday dtstart published updated">1993-08-16</span>)</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="white-space: nowrap;"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_release_life_cycle" title="Software release life cycle">Latest release</a></th><td class="infobox-data">13.7<sup about="#mwt9" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-wikidata-73981e2cad504468a6efbeb96fc329d5e243c125-v20_1-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;wikidata-73981e2cad504468a6efbeb96fc329d5e243c125-v20&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-wikidata-73981e2cad504468a6efbeb96fc329d5e243c125-v20-1&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-wikidata-73981e2cad504468a6efbeb96fc329d5e243c125-v20-1" id="mwDA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDg">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDw">]</span></span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Entity">&nbsp;</span><span class="mw-valign-text-top" typeof="mw:File/Frameless" data-mw="{&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Edit this on Wikidata&quot;}"><a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7715973?uselang=en#P348" title="Edit this on Wikidata"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:OOjs_UI_icon_edit-ltr-progressive.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/8a/OOjs_UI_icon_edit-ltr-progressive.svg/20px-OOjs_UI_icon_edit-ltr-progressive.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="Edit this on Wikidata" data-file-width="20" data-file-height="20" data-file-type="drawing" height="10" width="10" class="mw-file-element"></a></span> "Trixie" / 12 September 2026<span class="noprint"><span typeof="mw:Entity">;</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>25 days ago</span><span style="display:none"><span typeof="mw:Entity">&nbsp;</span>(<span class="bday dtstart published updated">12 September 2026</span>)</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="white-space: nowrap;"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_release_life_cycle" title="Software release life cycle">Latest preview</a></th><td class="infobox-data">14 "Forky"<sup about="#mwt14" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-2&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-2" id="mwEA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEg">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEw">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="white-space: nowrap;"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Repository_(version_control)" title="Repository (version control)">Repository</a></th><td class="infobox-data"><span class="url"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://deb.debian.org/" class="external text">deb<wbr>.debian<wbr>.org</a></span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="white-space: nowrap;">Marketing target</th><td class="infobox-data">General-purpose</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="white-space: nowrap;">Available in</th><td class="infobox-data">77 languages<sup about="#mwt19" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-3&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-3" id="mwFA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFg">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFw">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr><tr><td colspan="2" class="infobox-full-data"><span class="mw-empty-elt"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1214851843" about="#mwt22" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Template:Hidden begin/styles.css&quot;}}"></span><div class="hidden-begin mw-collapsible mw-collapsed mw-made-collapsible" style="   "><button type="button" class="mw-collapsible-toggle mw-collapsible-toggle-default mw-collapsible-toggle-collapsed" aria-expanded="false" tabindex="0"><span class="mw-collapsible-text">show</span></button><div class="hidden-title skin-nightmode-reset-color" style="  ">List of languages</div><div class="hidden-content mw-collapsible-content" style="  " hidden="until-found">Languages available in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debian-Installer" title="Debian-Installer">Debian-Installer</a>: Amharic, Arabic, Asturian, Belarusian, Bulgarian, Bengali, Tibetan, Bosnian, Catalan, Czech, Welsh, Danish, German, Dzongkha, Greek, English, Esperanto, Spanish, Estonian, Basque, Persian, Finnish, French, Irish, Galician, Gujarati, Hebrew, Croatian, Hungarian, Indonesian, Icelandic, Italian, Japanese, Georgian, Kabyle, Kazakh, Khmer, Kannada, Korean, Kurdish, Lao, Lithuanian, Latvian, Malagasy, Macedonian, Malayalam, Marathi, Burmese, Norwegian Bokmal, Norwegian Nynorsk, Nepali, Dutch, Occitan, Punjabi (Gurmukhi), Polish, Portuguese, Portuguese (Brazil), Romanian, Russian, Northern Sami, Sinhala, Slovak, Slovenian, Albanian, Serbian, Swedish, Tamil, Telugu, Tajik, Thai, Tagalog, Turkish, Uyghur, Ukrainian, Vietnamese, Chinese (Simplified), and Chinese (Traditional)<sup about="#mwt25" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-4&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-4" id="mwGA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwGQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGg">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGw">]</span></span></a></sup></div></div></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="white-space: nowrap;">Update method</th><td class="infobox-data"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/APT_(software)" title="APT (software)">APT</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="white-space: nowrap;"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Package_manager" title="Package manager">Package manager</a></th><td class="infobox-data"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dpkg" title="Dpkg">dpkg</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="white-space: nowrap;">Instruction sets</th><td class="infobox-data"><span class="mw-empty-elt"><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1126788409" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt28" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Plainlist/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}">.mw-parser-output .plainlist ol,.mw-parser-output .plainlist ul{line-height:inherit;list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.mw-parser-output .plainlist ol li,.mw-parser-output .plainlist ul li{margin-bottom:0}</style></span><div class="plainlist"><ul><li><b><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux_kernel" title="Linux kernel">Linux</a>:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amd64" title="Amd64" class="mw-redirect">amd64</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arm64" title="Arm64" class="mw-redirect">arm64</a>, armel, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armhf" title="Armhf" class="mw-redirect">armhf</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ppc64el" title="Ppc64el" class="mw-redirect">ppc64el</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RISC-V" title="RISC-V">riscv64</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S390x" title="S390x" class="mw-redirect">s390x</a><sup about="#mwt31" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-trixie-supported-architectures_5-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;trixie-supported-architectures&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-trixie-supported-architectures-5&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-trixie-supported-architectures-5" id="mwHA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwHQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHg">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHw">]</span></span></a></sup></li><li><b><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hurd" title="Hurd" class="mw-redirect">Hurd</a>:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amd64" title="Amd64" class="mw-redirect">amd64</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I386" title="I386">i386</a><sup about="#mwt36" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-6&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-6" id="mwIA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwIQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIg">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIw">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul></div></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="white-space: nowrap;"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kernel_(operating_system)" title="Kernel (operating system)">Kernel</a> type</th><td class="infobox-data"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monolithic_kernel" title="Monolithic kernel">Monolithic</a> (Linux)<br><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microkernel" title="Microkernel">Micro</a> (Hurd)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="white-space: nowrap;"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_space_and_kernel_space" title="User space and kernel space">Userland</a></th><td class="infobox-data"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GNU_Core_Utilities" title="GNU Core Utilities">GNU Core Utilities</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="white-space: nowrap;"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_interface" title="User interface">Default<br>user interface</a></th><td class="infobox-data"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GNOME" title="GNOME">GNOME</a><sup about="#mwt41" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-7&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-7" id="mwJA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwJQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJg">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJw">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="white-space: nowrap;"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_license" title="Software license">License</a></th><td class="infobox-data"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Free_software_license" title="Free software license" class="mw-redirect">Free licenses</a> compliant with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Open_Source_Definition#Debian_Free_Software_Guidelines" title="The Open Source Definition">DFSG</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="white-space: nowrap;">Official website</th><td class="infobox-data"><span class="url"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.debian.org/" class="external text">debian.org</a></span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="white-space: nowrap;">Tagline</th><td class="infobox-data">The Universal Operating System</td></tr></tbody></table>

<p id="mwKA"><b id="mwKQ">Debian</b> (<span class="rt-commentedText nowrap" about="#mwt44" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwKg" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;IPAc-en&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:IPAc-en&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ˈ&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;d&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ɛ&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;b&quot;},&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;i&quot;},&quot;6&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;ə&quot;},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;n&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="IPA nopopups noexcerpt" lang="en-fonipa"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:IPA/English" title="Help:IPA/English">/<span style="border-bottom:1px dotted"><span title="/ˈ/: primary stress follows">ˈ</span><span title="'d' in 'dye'">d</span><span title="/ɛ/: 'e' in 'dress'">ɛ</span><span title="'b' in 'buy'">b</span><span title="/i/: 'y' in 'happy'">i</span><span title="/ə/: 'a' in 'about'">ə</span><span title="'n' in 'nigh'">n</span></span>/</a></span></span>)<sup about="#mwt47" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-8&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-8" id="mwKw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLQ">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLg">]</span></span></a></sup> is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Free_software" title="Free software" id="mwLw">free</a>, general-purpose <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operating_system" title="Operating system" id="mwMA">operating system</a> developed by the Debian Project, a worldwide volunteer association founded by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ian_Murdock" title="Ian Murdock" id="mwMQ">Ian Murdock</a> on August 16, 1993.<sup about="#mwt50" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-what-is-debian-project_9-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;what-is-debian-project&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-what-is-debian-project-9&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-what-is-debian-project-9" id="mwMg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwMw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNA">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt53" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-10" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-10&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-10" id="mwNg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwNw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOA">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOQ">]</span></span></a></sup> It is the second-oldest <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux_distribution" title="Linux distribution" id="mwOg">Linux distribution</a> still being developed (only <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slackware" title="Slackware" id="mwOw">Slackware</a> is older)<sup about="#mwt56" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-11" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-11&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-11" id="mwPA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwPQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPg">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPw">]</span></span></a></sup> and forms the base of many others.<sup about="#mwt59" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-12" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-12&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-12" id="mwQA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwQQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQg">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwRA">It is deployed across <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Server_(computing)" title="Server (computing)" id="mwRQ">servers</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Personal_computers" title="Personal computers" class="mw-redirect" id="mwRg">personal computers</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embedded_devices" title="Embedded devices" class="mw-redirect" id="mwRw">embedded devices</a>. Among Linux distributions, it ranks second only to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ubuntu" title="Ubuntu" id="mwSA">Ubuntu</a> (a Debian derivative), with 16% of the overall market. According to the 2025 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stack_Overflow" title="Stack Overflow" id="mwSQ">Stack Overflow</a> Developer Survey, 11.4% of developers use it as their primary personal operating system and 10.4% professionally.<sup about="#mwt62" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-13" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-13&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-13" id="mwSg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwSw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTA">[</span>13<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Its emphasis on stability and long-term support over frequent package updates has made it prevalent in server and embedded deployments.<sup about="#mwt65" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-14" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-14&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-14" id="mwTg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwTw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUA">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwUg">Development is led by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debian_Project_Leader" title="Debian Project Leader" class="mw-redirect" id="mwUw">Project Leader</a> and guided by two foundational documents:<sup about="#mwt76" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-15" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-15&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-15" id="mwVA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwVQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVg">[</span>15<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVw">]</span></span></a></sup> the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debian_Social_Contract" title="Debian Social Contract" id="mwWA">Debian Social Contract</a>, a summary of the project's commitments that includes the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debian_Free_Software_Guidelines" title="Debian Free Software Guidelines" class="mw-redirect" id="mwWQ">Debian Free Software Guidelines</a> (DFSG),<sup about="#mwt79" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-social-contract_16-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;social-contract&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-social-contract-16&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-social-contract-16" id="mwWg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwWw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwXA">[</span>16<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwXQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt82" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-17" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-17&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-17" id="mwXg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwXw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYA">[</span>17<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYQ">]</span></span></a></sup> and the Debian Constitution, which describes the organizational structure.<sup about="#mwt85" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-constitution_18-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;constitution&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-constitution-18&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-constitution-18" id="mwYg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwYw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwZA">[</span>18<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwZQ">]</span></span></a></sup> The project publishes three concurrent development <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Branching_(version_control)" title="Branching (version control)" id="mwZg">branches</a>: <style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r886049734" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt66" id="mwZw" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;stable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">.mw-parser-output .monospaced{font-family:monospace,monospace}</style><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt66" id="mwaA">stable</span>, <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt68" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwaQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;testing&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt68" id="mwag">testing</span>, and <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt70" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwaw" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;unstable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt70" id="mwbA">unstable</span>, which correspond to different levels of software maturity. The current <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt72" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwbQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;stable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt72" id="mwbg">stable</span> release, released on August 9, 2025 and codenamed "Trixie",<sup about="#mwt88" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-trixie-released_19-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;trixie-released&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-trixie-released-19&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-trixie-released-19" id="mwbw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwcA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcQ">[</span>19<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcg">]</span></span></a></sup> includes tens of thousands of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Package_format" title="Package format" id="mwcw">packages</a> maintained by more than a thousand active contributors.<sup about="#mwt91" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-20" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-20&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-20" id="mwdA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwdQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdg">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt94" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-trixie-packages-number_21-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;trixie-packages-number&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-trixie-packages-number-21&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-trixie-packages-number-21" id="mweA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mweQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mweg">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwew">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwfA">Since 1997, the project has operated independently through <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_in_the_Public_Interest" title="Software in the Public Interest" id="mwfQ">Software in the Public Interest</a>, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-profit_corporation" title="Non-profit corporation" class="mw-redirect" id="mwfg">non-profit corporation</a> founded by project members to hold its assets and trademarks.<sup about="#mwt97" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-spi_22-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;spi&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-spi-22&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-spi-22" id="mwfw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwgA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgQ">[</span>22<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt98" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-what-is-debian-project_9-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;what-is-debian-project&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-what-is-debian-project-9" id="mwgw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwhA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwhQ">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwhg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt101" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-23" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-23&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-23" id="mwhw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwiA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwiQ">[</span>23<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwig">]</span></span></a></sup> It previously received support from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Free_Software_Foundation" title="Free Software Foundation" id="mwiw">Free Software Foundation</a> between 1994 and 1995, with the sponsorship ending due to disagreements.<sup about="#mwt104" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-debian-and-fsf_24-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;debian-and-fsf&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-debian-and-fsf-24&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-debian-and-fsf-24" id="mwjA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwjQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwjg">[</span>24<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwjw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt107" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-fsf-and-debian-separate_25-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;fsf-and-debian-separate&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-fsf-and-debian-separate-25&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-fsf-and-debian-separate-25" id="mwkA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwkQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwkg">[</span>25<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwkw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" id="mwlA" data-mw="{&quot;autoGenerated&quot;:true}"></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwlQ" aria-labelledby="History"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="History">History</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: History"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwlg" aria-labelledby="Version_history"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Version_history">Version history</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section: Version history"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt108" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwlw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Further&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Further&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Debian release version history&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1368532237" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt109" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}">.mw-parser-output .hatnote{font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output div.hatnote{padding-left:1.6em;margin-bottom:0.5em}.mw-parser-output .hatnote i{font-style:normal}.mw-parser-output .hatnote+.mw-empty-elt+.hatnote{margin-top:-0.5em}@media print{body.ns-0 .mw-parser-output .hatnote{display:none!important}}</style></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt108" id="mwmA">Further information: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debian_release_version_history" title="Debian release version history">Debian release version history</a></div>

<p id="mwmQ">Debian uses version numbers and code names based on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Toy_Story_characters" title="List of Toy Story characters" id="mwmg">characters</a> of the <i id="mwmw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toy_Story_(franchise)" title="Toy Story (franchise)" id="mwnA">Toy Story</a></i> franchise to refer to its releases.<sup about="#mwt112" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-26" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-26&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-26" id="mwnQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwng"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwnw">[</span>26<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwoA">]</span></span></a></sup> This naming convention was introduced by former project leader <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruce_Perens" title="Bruce Perens" id="mwoQ">Bruce Perens</a>, who was working at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pixar" title="Pixar" id="mwog">Pixar</a> at the time. The unstable branch is permanently named after <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sid_Phillips_(Toy_Story)" title="Sid Phillips (Toy Story)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwow">Sid</a>, the neighborhood child known for destroying toys.<sup about="#mwt115" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-27" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-27&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-27" id="mwpA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwpQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwpg">[</span>27<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwpw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwqA" aria-labelledby="Founding_(1993–1999)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Founding_(1993–1999)"><span id="Founding_.281993.E2.80.931999.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Founding (1993–1999)</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3" title="Edit section: Founding (1993–1999)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mwqQ" aria-labelledby="Debian_Linux_Manifesto_(1993)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Debian_Linux_Manifesto_(1993)"><span id="Debian_Linux_Manifesto_.281993.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Debian Linux Manifesto (1993)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4" title="Edit section: Debian Linux Manifesto (1993)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwqg"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:IanMurdock_(cropped).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwqw"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:IanMurdock_(cropped).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/IanMurdock_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-IanMurdock_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/IanMurdock_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-IanMurdock_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1605" data-file-height="2087" data-file-type="bitmap" height="195" width="150" class="mw-file-element" id="mwrA"></a><figcaption id="mwrQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ian_Murdock" title="Ian Murdock" id="mwrg">Ian Murdock</a>, Debian's founder, in 2008</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwrw">The first public mention of the project occurred on August 16, 1993, when <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ian_Murdock" title="Ian Murdock" id="mwsA">Ian Murdock</a> posted an announcement to the <i id="mwsQ">comp.os.linux.development</i> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Usenet_newsgroup" title="Usenet newsgroup" id="mwsg">newsgroup</a>. Murdock founded the project due to his dissatisfaction with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Softlanding_Linux_System" title="Softlanding Linux System" id="mwsw">Softlanding Linux System</a>; after making extensive modifications to this system, he concluded that it would be more efficient to develop a new distribution from scratch.<sup about="#mwt118" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-28" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-28&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-28" id="mwtA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwtQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwtg">[</span>28<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwtw">]</span></span></a></sup> Similar to the original announcement of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux_kernel" title="Linux kernel" id="mwuA">Linux</a>, Murdock's post solicited feedback and suggestions on how the system could be improved.<sup about="#mwt121" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-29" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-29&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-29" id="mwuQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwug"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwuw">[</span>29<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt124" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-30" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-30&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-30" id="mwvQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwvg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvw">[</span>30<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwwA">]</span></span></a></sup> The name <i id="mwwQ">Debian</i> was a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portmanteau" title="Portmanteau" id="mwwg">portmanteau</a> of his first name and that of his then-wife, Deborah Lynn.<!-- If you want to state that Deborah was his girlfriend at the time, cite a source --><sup about="#mwt127" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-31" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-31&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-31" id="mwww"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwxA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxQ">[</span>31<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwxw">The first internal release, pre-alpha 0.01, came out on September 15, 1993. The first public versions, beta 0.90 and beta 0.91, followed on January 26 and 29, 1994, respectively,<sup about="#mwt130" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-32" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-32&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-32" id="mwyA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwyQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyg">[</span>32<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyw">]</span></span></a></sup> with their mailing lists hosted by Pixar.<sup about="#mwt133" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-33" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-33&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-33" id="mwzA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwzQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwzg">[</span>33<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwzw">]</span></span></a></sup> These releases included the Debian Linux Manifesto, in which Murdock outlined his vision for the project, advocating for a distribution "developed openly in the spirit of Linux and GNU".<sup about="#mwt136" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-34" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-34&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-34" id="mw0A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw0Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw0g">[</span>34<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw0w">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mw1A" aria-labelledby="Free_Software_Foundation_sponsorship_(1994–1995)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Free_Software_Foundation_sponsorship_(1994–1995)"><span id="Free_Software_Foundation_sponsorship_.281994.E2.80.931995.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Free Software Foundation sponsorship (1994–1995)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5" title="Edit section: Free Software Foundation sponsorship (1994–1995)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mw1Q">Between November 1994 and November 1995, the project was sponsored by the Free Software Foundation (FSF),<sup about="#mwt137" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-what-is-debian-project_9-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;what-is-debian-project&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-what-is-debian-project-9" id="mw1g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw1w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw2A">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw2Q">]</span></span></a></sup> whose sponsorship Murdock sought with the hope that it would also give the FSF experience in packaging a complete <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GNU" title="GNU" id="mw2g">GNU</a> system. In March 1995, Murdock stepped down as project leader to dedicate more time to his studies, work, and family; the new team<!-- Do not explicitly state "Bruce Perens" because he is not mentioned in the source --> did not seek to continue the sponsorship.<sup about="#mwt138" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-fsf-and-debian-separate_25-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;fsf-and-debian-separate&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-fsf-and-debian-separate-25" id="mw2w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw3A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw3Q">[</span>25<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw3g">]</span></span></a></sup> While the Debian Project remained aligned with the FSF's political and philosophical goals, differences in technical direction ended the arrangement, with the FSF invited to continue participating in the project on the same basis as individual developers and other contributing organizations.<sup about="#mwt139" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-debian-and-fsf_24-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;debian-and-fsf&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-debian-and-fsf-24" id="mw3w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw4A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw4Q">[</span>24<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw4g">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="6" id="mw4w" aria-labelledby="Bruce_Perens_as_project_leader_(1996–1997)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Bruce_Perens_as_project_leader_(1996–1997)"><span id="Bruce_Perens_as_project_leader_.281996.E2.80.931997.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Bruce Perens as project leader (1996–1997)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6" title="Edit section: Bruce Perens as project leader (1996–1997)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mw5A"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3541705843_f896546bec_o_crop.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mw5Q"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3541705843_f896546bec_o_crop.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/3541705843_f896546bec_o_crop.jpg/250px-3541705843_f896546bec_o_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/3541705843_f896546bec_o_crop.jpg/500px-3541705843_f896546bec_o_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1651" data-file-height="1782" data-file-type="bitmap" height="189" width="175" class="mw-file-element" id="mw5g"></a><figcaption id="mw5w"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruce_Perens" title="Bruce Perens" id="mw6A">Bruce Perens</a>, Debian project leader who drafted the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debian_Social_Contract" title="Debian Social Contract" id="mw6Q">Debian Social Contract</a></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mw6g">In April 1996, Bruce Perens became the project leader.<sup about="#mwt145" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-leaders_35-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;leaders&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-leaders-35&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-leaders-35" id="mw6w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw7A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw7Q">[</span>35<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw7g">]</span></span></a></sup> On June 17 of the same year, Debian 1.1 "Buzz" was released,<sup about="#mwt148" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-36" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-36&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-36" id="mw7w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw8A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw8Q">[</span>36<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw8g">]</span></span></a></sup> the first release under his leadership. By that time, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ian_Jackson_(computer_programmer)" title="Ian Jackson (computer programmer)" id="mw8w">Ian Jackson's</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dpkg" title="Dpkg" id="mw9A">dpkg</a> had already become an integral part of Debian.<sup about="#mwt140" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKrafft200531–32_37-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKrafft200531–32&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKrafft200531–32-37&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Krafft&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2005&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;31–32&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKrafft200531–32-37" id="mw9Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw9g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw9w">[</span>37<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw-A">]</span></span></a></sup> The concept of a social contract with the free software community was suggested to Perens by Ean Schussler; Perens composed a draft, which was subsequently refined by Debian developers through email discussion over most of June and approved by vote, producing the Debian Social Contract and the DFSG, published on July 4, 1997.<sup about="#mwt151" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-38" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-38&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-38" id="mw-Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw-g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw-w">[</span>38<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw_A">]</span></span></a></sup> He created <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BusyBox" title="BusyBox" id="mw_Q">BusyBox</a> to enable running the installer from a single <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Floppy_disk" title="Floppy disk" id="mw_g">floppy disk</a>.<sup about="#mwt154" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-39" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-39&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-39" id="mw_w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQE">[</span>39<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQI">]</span></span></a></sup> By the time Debian 1.2 "Rex" was released on December 12, 1996,<sup about="#mwt157" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-releases-exact-date_40-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;releases-exact-date&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-releases-exact-date-40&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-releases-exact-date-40" id="mwAQM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQU">[</span>40<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQY">]</span></span></a></sup> the project had grown to nearly 200 volunteers.<sup about="#mwt160" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-41" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-41&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-41" id="mwAQc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQk">[</span>41<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQo">]</span></span></a></sup> Perens stepped down as project leader in December 1997 and left the project entirely on March 18, 1998.<sup about="#mwt161" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-leaders_35-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;leaders&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-leaders-35" id="mwAQs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQ0">[</span>35<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQ4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt164" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-42" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-42&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-42" id="mwAQ8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARE">[</span>42<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="7" id="mwARM" aria-labelledby="Formation_of_Software_in_the_Public_Interest_(1997)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Formation_of_Software_in_the_Public_Interest_(1997)"><span id="Formation_of_Software_in_the_Public_Interest_.281997.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Formation of Software in the Public Interest (1997)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7" title="Edit section: Formation of Software in the Public Interest (1997)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwARQ">On June 16, 1997, following the end of the FSF sponsorship, Debian motivated the formation of Software in the Public Interest (SPI), a non-profit corporation registered in the state of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_(state)" title="New York (state)" id="mwARU">New York</a>. SPI was founded to help Debian and other similar organizations develop and distribute <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Open_hardware" title="Open hardware" class="mw-redirect" id="mwARY">open hardware</a> and software, acting as a fiscal sponsor by handling non-technical administrative tasks so that projects are not required to operate their own <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Legal_entity" title="Legal entity" class="mw-redirect" id="mwARc">legal entity</a>.<sup about="#mwt165" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-spi_22-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;spi&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-spi-22" id="mwARg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARo">[</span>22<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="8" id="mwARw" aria-labelledby="Ian_Jackson_and_Wichert_Akkerman_leadership_(1998–1999)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Ian_Jackson_and_Wichert_Akkerman_leadership_(1998–1999)"><span id="Ian_Jackson_and_Wichert_Akkerman_leadership_.281998.E2.80.931999.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Ian Jackson and Wichert Akkerman leadership (1998–1999)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8" title="Edit section: Ian Jackson and Wichert Akkerman leadership (1998–1999)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAR0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ian_Jackson_(computer_programmer)" title="Ian Jackson (computer programmer)" id="mwAR4">Ian Jackson</a> became project leader in January 1998.<sup about="#mwt166" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-leaders_35-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;leaders&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-leaders-35" id="mwAR8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASE">[</span>35<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASI">]</span></span></a></sup> Debian 2.0 "Hamm", released on July 24, 1998, was the first multi-architecture release of Debian, adding support for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Motorola_68000_family" title="Motorola 68000 family" class="mw-redirect" id="mwASM">Motorola 68000 family</a>.<sup about="#mwt169" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-releases_43-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;releases&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-releases-43&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-releases-43" id="mwASQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASY">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASc">]</span></span></a></sup> On December 2, 1998, the Debian Constitution was ratified for the first time,<sup about="#mwt172" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-44" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-44&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-44" id="mwASg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASo">[</span>44<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASs">]</span></span></a></sup> simultaneously initiating the election process that would result in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Debian_project_leaders#Wichert_Akkerman" title="List of Debian project leaders" id="mwASw">Wichert Akkerman</a> succeeding Jackson as project leader in January 1999.<sup about="#mwt175" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-45" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-45&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-45" id="mwAS0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAS4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAS8">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATA">]</span></span></a></sup> On March 9, 1999, Debian 2.1 "Slink" was released, alongside the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Package_manager" title="Package manager" id="mwATE">package manager</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Front_end_and_back_end" title="Front end and back end" id="mwATI">front-end</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/APT_(software)" title="APT (software)" id="mwATM">APT</a>.<sup about="#mwt176" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-releases-exact-date_40-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;releases-exact-date&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-releases-exact-date-40" id="mwATQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATY">[</span>40<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt177" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-releases_43-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;releases&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-releases-43" id="mwATg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATo">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATs">]</span></span></a></sup> On May 23, 1999, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internal_Revenue_Service" title="Internal Revenue Service" id="mwATw">Internal Revenue Service</a> determined that SPI qualifies for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/501(c)(3)" title="501(c)(3)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAT0">501(c)(3)</a> status, allowing the Debian Project to accept <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tax_deductible" title="Tax deductible" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAT4">tax deductible</a> contributions in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States" title="United States" id="mwAT8">United States</a>.<sup about="#mwt180" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-46" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-46&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-46" id="mwAUA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUI">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="9" id="mwAUQ" aria-labelledby="Consolidation_(2000–2004)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Consolidation_(2000–2004)"><span id="Consolidation_.282000.E2.80.932004.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Consolidation (2000–2004)</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9" title="Edit section: Consolidation (2000–2004)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="10" id="mwAUU" aria-labelledby="Package_pools_and_the_testing_branch_(2000)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Package_pools_and_the_testing_branch_(2000)"><span id="Package_pools_and_the_testing_branch_.282000.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Package pools and the testing branch (2000)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10" title="Edit section: Package pools and the testing branch (2000)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAUY">On December 13, 2000, Debian activated package pools on its ftp-master archive server,<sup about="#mwt183" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-47" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-47&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-47" id="mwAUc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUk">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUo">]</span></span></a></sup> allowing the "Woody" release to be prepared. A package pool is a collection of a package's versions, which Debian's branches draw from for their packages. This change enabled special-purpose distributions, including a new testing branch that was used to prepare "Woody" for release. Under this system, packages in the unstable branch considered to be sufficiently reliable were promoted to testing after a waiting period of several weeks, a mechanism intended to reduce freeze time and allow the project to prepare a new release at any point.<sup about="#mwt186" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-48" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-48&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-48" id="mwAUs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAU0">[</span>48<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAU4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="11" id="mwAU8" aria-labelledby="First_DebConf_(2000)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="First_DebConf_(2000)"><span id="First_DebConf_.282000.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>First DebConf (2000)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11" title="Edit section: First DebConf (2000)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAVA">The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debian_Conference" title="Debian Conference" id="mwAVE">Debian Conference</a> was held in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bordeaux" title="Bordeaux" id="mwAVI">Bordeaux</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/France" title="France" id="mwAVM">France</a>, from July 5 to 9, 2000. The event brought Debian developers and advanced users together in person for the first time, giving the Debian project a physical presence rather than existing solely as an online collective. In addition to working sessions, the conference served as a venue for attendees to meet other members of the free software community, with some presentations open to the general public. Discussion topics included the Debian user base and its adoption in corporate settings and derived distributions, ongoing development of "Woody", the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debian_GNU/Hurd" title="Debian GNU/Hurd" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAVQ">Debian GNU/Hurd</a> port, the project's quality-control processes, the procedure for becoming a Debian developer, and tools such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debconf" title="Debconf" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAVU">debconf</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boot_disk" title="Boot disk" id="mwAVY">boot-floppies</a>. The program combined presentations, technical talks, birds-of-a-feather sessions, and coding parties.<sup about="#mwt189" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-49" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-49&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-49" id="mwAVc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAVg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVk">[</span>49<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="12" id="mwAVs" aria-labelledby="HP's_adoption_of_Debian_(2001)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="HP's_adoption_of_Debian_(2001)"><span id="HP.27s_adoption_of_Debian_.282001.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>HP's adoption of Debian (2001)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12" title="Edit section: HP's adoption of Debian (2001)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAVw">In May 2001, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hewlett-Packard" title="Hewlett-Packard" id="mwAV0">Hewlett-Packard</a> (HP) announced that it would use Debian for its future Linux development work. Martin Fink, HP's general manager of Linux systems operations, said the company chose Debian because it was the most free and open Linux distribution available, a factor he believed would help prevent <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proprietary_software" title="Proprietary software" id="mwAV4">proprietary software</a> from dominating efforts to establish a standardized Linux platform, since Debian was not controlled by a single commercial entity. Debian developer Bruce Perens, who acted as HP's Linux advocate, disclosed the decision in an email to the Debian development mailing list, noting that HP had already begun distributing Debian to customers and planned to offer support and training for it. Perens described the move as an initial step toward HP's broader support for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux_Standard_Base" title="Linux Standard Base" id="mwAV8">Linux Standard Base</a> project.<sup about="#mwt192" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-50" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-50&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-50" id="mwAWA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAWE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWI">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="13" id="mwAWQ" aria-labelledby="Debian_&quot;Woody&quot;_release_(2002)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Debian_&quot;Woody&quot;_release_(2002)"><span id="Debian_.22Woody.22_release_.282002.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Debian "Woody" release (2002)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13" title="Edit section: Debian &quot;Woody&quot; release (2002)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAWU"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Debian-Woody.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAWY"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Debian-Woody.png" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Debian-Woody.png/250px-Debian-Woody.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Debian-Woody.png/500px-Debian-Woody.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1024" data-file-height="768" data-file-type="bitmap" height="169" width="225" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAWc"></a><figcaption id="mwAWg">Debian 3 "Woody", 2002</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAWk">Debian 3 "Woody" was released on July 19, 2002, expanding the project's scope. Supported by a community of over 900 developers and led by newly appointed Project Leader <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bdale_Garbee" title="Bdale Garbee" id="mwAWo">Bdale Garbee</a>, the release included approximately 8,500 binary packages distributed across seven official binary CDs. This version broadened hardware compatibility by introducing support for several new architectures, including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IA-64" title="IA-64" id="mwAWs">IA-64</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HP_PA-RISC" title="HP PA-RISC" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAWw">HP PA-RISC</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MIPS_architecture" title="MIPS architecture" id="mwAW0">MIPS</a> (both big and little endian), and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S/390" title="S/390" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAW4">S/390</a>. It was the first Debian release to incorporate <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cryptographic_software" title="Cryptographic software" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAW8">cryptographic software</a>, following the relaxation of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Export_of_cryptography" title="Export of cryptography" id="mwAXA">Cold War US cryptography export restrictions</a>, as well as the first to feature the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/K_Desktop_Environment_3" title="K Desktop Environment 3" id="mwAXE">KDE desktop environment</a> after its <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qt_(software)" title="Qt (software)" id="mwAXI">Qt</a> licensing issues were resolved.<sup about="#mwt193" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-releases_43-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;releases&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-releases-43" id="mwAXM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXU">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="14" id="mwAXc" aria-labelledby="University_of_Twente_server_fire_(2002)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="University_of_Twente_server_fire_(2002)"><span id="University_of_Twente_server_fire_.282002.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>University of Twente server fire (2002)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14" title="Edit section: University of Twente server fire (2002)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAXg">On November 20, 2002, a fire destroyed the network operations center at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Twente" title="University of Twente" id="mwAXk">University of Twente</a> in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Netherlands" title="Netherlands" id="mwAXo">Netherlands</a>, which hosted one of Debian's servers, satie.debian.org. The blaze broke out around 8:00 a.m. local time and consumed the building so thoroughly that firefighters could not save the server room. Because satie had hosted the project's security archive, its non-US archive, and the databases supporting new-maintainer applications and quality assurance, the corresponding services (security.debian.org, non-us.debian.org, nm.debian.org, and qa.debian.org) went offline as a result.<sup about="#mwt196" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-51" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-51&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-51" id="mwAXs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAX0">[</span>51<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAX4">]</span></span></a></sup> Debian subsequently rebuilt these services on another host, klecker, which had recently been relocated from the United States to the Netherlands.<sup about="#mwt199" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-52" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-52&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-52" id="mwAX8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAYA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYE">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="15" id="mwAYM" aria-labelledby="Ubuntu_fork_and_the_compatibility_debate_(2004)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Ubuntu_fork_and_the_compatibility_debate_(2004)"><span id="Ubuntu_fork_and_the_compatibility_debate_.282004.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Ubuntu fork and the compatibility debate (2004)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15" title="Edit section: Ubuntu fork and the compatibility debate (2004)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAYQ">On October 20, 2004, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Shuttleworth" title="Mark Shuttleworth" id="mwAYU">Mark Shuttleworth</a> announced the first release of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ubuntu" title="Ubuntu" id="mwAYY">Ubuntu</a>, a new Debian-derived distribution aimed at combining Debian's extensive package base with a faster installer, a fixed six-month release cycle, and 18 months of security support per release, under the version 4.10 and the codename "Warty Warthog".<sup about="#mwt202" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-53" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-53&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-53" id="mwAYc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAYg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYk">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYo">]</span></span></a></sup> The rapid growth of Ubuntu sparked debate within the Debian community regarding the long-term compatibility of Debian-derived distributions. Some Debian developers warned that as more developers began building packages targeting Ubuntu rather than Debian proper, divergence between the two could erode that compatibility, mimicking the fragmentation seen among <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RPM_Package_Manager" title="RPM Package Manager" id="mwAYs">RPM</a>-based distributions. Other community members argued that Debian should address its lengthy release cycles, calling for a predictable, time-based release schedule similar to that adopted by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GNOME_Project" title="GNOME Project" id="mwAYw">GNOME Project</a>, in order to reduce the incentive for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Downstream_(software_development)" title="Downstream (software development)" id="mwAY0">downstream</a> distributions to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fork_(software_development)" title="Fork (software development)" id="mwAY4">fork</a>.<sup about="#mwt205" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-54" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-54&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-54" id="mwAY8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZE">[</span>54<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="16" id="mwAZM" aria-labelledby="Maturity_and_controversies_(2005–2015)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Maturity_and_controversies_(2005–2015)"><span id="Maturity_and_controversies_.282005.E2.80.932015.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Maturity and controversies (2005–2015)</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16" title="Edit section: Maturity and controversies (2005–2015)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="17" id="mwAZQ" aria-labelledby="Debian_3.1_&quot;Sarge&quot;_release_(2005)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Debian_3.1_&quot;Sarge&quot;_release_(2005)"><span id="Debian_3.1_.22Sarge.22_release_.282005.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Debian 3.1 "Sarge" release (2005)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17" title="Edit section: Debian 3.1 &quot;Sarge&quot; release (2005)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAZU"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Debian-Sarge.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAZY"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Debian-Sarge.png" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Debian-Sarge.png/250px-Debian-Sarge.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Debian-Sarge.png/500px-Debian-Sarge.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1024" data-file-height="768" data-file-type="bitmap" height="165" width="220" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAZc"></a><figcaption id="mwAZg">Debian 3.1 "Sarge"</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAZk">Debian 3.1 "Sarge" was released on 6 June 2005, shortly after Branden Robinson had been appointed Project Leader.<sup about="#mwt206" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-releases_43-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;releases&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-releases-43" id="mwAZo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZw">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZ0">]</span></span></a></sup> Sarge was the first release to include a complete <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Office_suite" title="Office suite" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAZ4">office suite</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenOffice.org#OpenOffice.org_1" title="OpenOffice.org" id="mwAZ8">OpenOffice.org 1.1</a>, and the first stable release to use the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debian-Installer" title="Debian-Installer" id="mwAaA">Debian-Installer</a>, replacing the older <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boot_disk" title="Boot disk" id="mwAaE">boot-floppies</a> method. The new installer featured a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Modular_design" title="Modular design" id="mwAaI">modular design</a> intended to support future extensibility and had been fully translated into almost forty languages. Additional features included improved hardware detection, support for booting from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/USB_flash_drive" title="USB flash drive" id="mwAaM">USB flash drives</a>, use of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aptitude_(software)" title="Aptitude (software)" id="mwAaQ">aptitude</a> for package installation during base system configuration, and support for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XFS" title="XFS" id="mwAaU">XFS file system</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RAID" title="RAID" id="mwAaY">RAID</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logical_volume_management" title="Logical volume management" id="mwAac">LVM</a>.<sup about="#mwt209" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-55" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-55&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-55" id="mwAag"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAak"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAao">[</span>55<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAas">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="18" id="mwAaw" aria-labelledby="Debian–Mozilla_trademark_dispute_(2006)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Debian–Mozilla_trademark_dispute_(2006)"><span id="Debian.E2.80.93Mozilla_trademark_dispute_.282006.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Debian–Mozilla trademark dispute (2006)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18" title="Edit section: Debian–Mozilla trademark dispute (2006)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt210" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAa0" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;main&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Main&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Debian–Mozilla trademark dispute&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt211" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt210" id="mwAa4">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debian–Mozilla_trademark_dispute" title="Debian–Mozilla trademark dispute">Debian–Mozilla trademark dispute</a></div>
<figure class="mw-halign-left" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAa8"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Iceweasel_icon.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAbA"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Iceweasel_icon.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Iceweasel_icon.svg/120px-Iceweasel_icon.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Iceweasel_icon.svg/250px-Iceweasel_icon.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="128" data-file-height="128" data-file-type="drawing" height="75" width="75" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAbE"></a><figcaption id="mwAbI"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iceweasel" title="Iceweasel" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAbM">Iceweasel</a> logo</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAbQ">In 2006, following a debate that began in 2004,<sup about="#mwt214" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-56" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-56&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-56" id="mwAbU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAbY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbc">[</span>56<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbg">]</span></span></a></sup> Mozilla's software was renamed in Debian for two reasons: the Firefox logo was under a proprietary license incompatible with the DFSG,<sup about="#mwt217" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-57" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-57&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-57" id="mwAbk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAbo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbs">[</span>57<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbw">]</span></span></a></sup> and a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mozilla_Corporation" title="Mozilla Corporation" id="mwAb0">Mozilla Corporation</a> representative stated that programs with unapproved modifications could not be distributed under its trademarks.<sup about="#mwt220" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-58" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-58&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-58" id="mwAb4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAb8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcA">[</span>58<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcE">]</span></span></a></sup> Because Debian applied security patches without prior approval from Mozilla, a practice consistent with its package maintenance policy, the project began distributing the browser <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firefox" title="Firefox" id="mwAcI">Firefox</a> as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iceweasel" title="Iceweasel" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAcM">Iceweasel</a>, the email client <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mozilla_Thunderbird" title="Mozilla Thunderbird" id="mwAcQ">Thunderbird</a> as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debian–Mozilla_trademark_dispute#Icedove" title="Debian–Mozilla trademark dispute" id="mwAcU">Icedove</a>, and the Internet suite <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SeaMonkey" title="SeaMonkey" id="mwAcY">SeaMonkey</a> as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debian–Mozilla_trademark_dispute#Iceape" title="Debian–Mozilla trademark dispute" id="mwAcc">Iceape</a>. The renamings were implemented in the unstable branch in 2006 and reached the stable release with the launch of Debian 4.0 "Etch" in 2007.<sup about="#mwt223" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-59" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-59&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-59" id="mwAcg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAck"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAco">[</span>59<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt226" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-60" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-60&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-60" id="mwAcw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAc0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAc4">[</span>60<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAc8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="19" id="mwAdA" aria-labelledby="Dunc-Tank_funding_controversy_(2006)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Dunc-Tank_funding_controversy_(2006)"><span id="Dunc-Tank_funding_controversy_.282006.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Dunc-Tank funding controversy (2006)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19" title="Edit section: Dunc-Tank funding controversy (2006)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAdE"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Debian_Etch-ja.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAdI"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Debian_Etch-ja.png" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Debian_Etch-ja.png/250px-Debian_Etch-ja.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Debian_Etch-ja.png/500px-Debian_Etch-ja.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1024" data-file-height="768" data-file-type="bitmap" height="169" width="225" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAdM"></a><figcaption id="mwAdQ">Debian 4 "Etch", 2007</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAdU">Debian 4.0 "Etch" was released on April 8, 2007,<sup about="#mwt227" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-releases-exact-date_40-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;releases-exact-date&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-releases-exact-date-40" id="mwAdY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAdc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdg">[</span>40<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdk">]</span></span></a></sup> following a delay caused by a protest by unpaid developers. The protest started in 2006 after two <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Release_management" title="Release management" id="mwAdo">release managers</a> accepted payment from Dunc-Tank, an organization composed entirely of project members, to accelerate Etch's release.<sup about="#mwt230" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-61" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-61&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-61" id="mwAds"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAdw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAd0">[</span>61<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAd4">]</span></span></a></sup> In response, some developers deliberately reduced their contributions to the project. Critics argued that the project had traditionally relied on voluntary work, and that introducing paid contributors created an inconsistency in which only two of roughly 1,000 developers would be compensated. Some also contended that if funding were to be introduced, it should be extended to all developers, since their contributions were considered equally important to those of the release managers.<sup about="#mwt233" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-62" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-62&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-62" id="mwAd8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAeA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeE">[</span>62<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="20" id="mwAeM" aria-labelledby="OpenSSL_predictable_key_vulnerability_(2008)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="OpenSSL_predictable_key_vulnerability_(2008)"><span id="OpenSSL_predictable_key_vulnerability_.282008.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>OpenSSL predictable key vulnerability (2008)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20" title="Edit section: OpenSSL predictable key vulnerability (2008)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAeQ">On May 13, 2008, Debian developer Luciano Bello discovered that the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenSSL" title="OpenSSL" id="mwAeU">OpenSSL</a> library distributed with Debian and derivatives such as Ubuntu generated security keys that were vulnerable to a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brute-force_attack" title="Brute-force attack" id="mwAeY">brute-force attack</a>.<sup about="#mwt236" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-63" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-63&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-63" id="mwAec"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAeg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAek">[</span>63<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeo">]</span></span></a></sup> Only 32,767 different keys were produced, making the cryptographic key material easily guessable. The weakness was caused by changes made in May 2006 by another Debian developer in response to warnings from the memory debugging tool <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valgrind" title="Valgrind" id="mwAes">Valgrind</a>, which indicated that OpenSSL was using memory that had not been initialized to a known state. Normally, using uninitialized memory in this way would be considered a programming error. In this case, however, the OpenSSL library was intentionally relying on that uninitialized memory as a source of randomness. As a result, removing the supposed error also removed the randomness the software depended on for key generation. Many key types were affected, including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SSH" title="SSH" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAew">SSH</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenVPN" title="OpenVPN" id="mwAe0">OpenVPN</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DNSSEC" title="DNSSEC" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAe4">DNSSEC</a> keys, as well as key material used in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X.509" title="X.509" id="mwAe8">X.509</a> certificates and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SSL/TLS" title="SSL/TLS" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAfA">SSL/TLS</a> sessions.<sup about="#mwt239" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-64" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-64&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-64" id="mwAfE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfM">[</span>64<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Resolving the issue was not simple, since patching the vulnerability alone was insufficient; all affected keys and certificates also had to be regenerated.<sup about="#mwt242" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-65" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-65&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-65" id="mwAfU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfc">[</span>65<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="21" id="mwAfk" aria-labelledby="Time-based_release_cycle_and_official_backports_(2009-2010)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Time-based_release_cycle_and_official_backports_(2009-2010)"><span id="Time-based_release_cycle_and_official_backports_.282009-2010.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Time-based release cycle and official backports (2009-2010)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21" title="Edit section: Time-based release cycle and official backports (2009-2010)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAfo">On July 29, 2009, Debian adopted a policy of time based development freezes on a two year cycle, under which freezes would occur in December of every odd numbered year, with releases following sometime in the first half of every even numbered year. This change was intended to provide better predictability of releases for users, allow developers to do better long term planning, give more time for disruptive changes so as to reduce inconvenience for users, and reduce overall freeze time.<sup about="#mwt245" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-two-year-cycle_66-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;two-year-cycle&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-two-year-cycle-66&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-two-year-cycle-66" id="mwAfs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAf0">[</span>66<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAf4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAf8">On September 5, 2010, the Debian <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backports" title="Backports" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAgA">backports</a> service became official. Backports are packages from the testing branch recompiled for the current stable or oldstable release, allowing users to install more recent versions of programs without sacrificing the overall stability of the system. The original service was created by Debian developer Norbert Tretkowski with support from team(ix), and was later further developed with the help of Debian developers Alexander Wirt and Jörg Jaspert.<sup about="#mwt248" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-67" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-67&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-67" id="mwAgE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgM">[</span>67<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="22" id="mwAgU" aria-labelledby="Debian_&quot;Squeeze&quot;_release_(2011)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Debian_&quot;Squeeze&quot;_release_(2011)"><span id="Debian_.22Squeeze.22_release_.282011.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Debian "Squeeze" release (2011)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=22" title="Edit section: Debian &quot;Squeeze&quot; release (2011)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAgY">Debian 6 "Squeeze", released on 6 February 2011, was the first version whose Linux kernel was distributed entirely without <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proprietary_firmware" title="Proprietary firmware" id="mwAgc">proprietary firmware</a>, with non-free components moved to a separate repository, allowing users to install them if needed. It was also the first release to come with two "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flavors" title="Flavors" class="mw-redirect mw-disambig" id="mwAgg">flavors</a>", Debian GNU/Linux and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debian_GNU/kFreeBSD" title="Debian GNU/kFreeBSD" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAgk">Debian GNU/kFreeBSD</a>, the latter introduced as a technology preview.<sup about="#mwt251" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-68" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-68&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-68" id="mwAgo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgw">[</span>68<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAg0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="23" id="mwAg4" aria-labelledby="Systemd_adoption_debate_(2014)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Systemd_adoption_debate_(2014)"><span id="Systemd_adoption_debate_.282014.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Systemd adoption debate (2014)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=23" title="Edit section: Systemd adoption debate (2014)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAg8"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Systemd_logo_(no_wordmark).svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAhA"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Systemd_logo_(no_wordmark).svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Systemd_logo_%28no_wordmark%29.svg/250px-Systemd_logo_%28no_wordmark%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Systemd_logo_%28no_wordmark%29.svg/330px-Systemd_logo_%28no_wordmark%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="86" data-file-height="26" data-file-type="drawing" height="45" width="150" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAhE"></a><figcaption id="mwAhI"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Systemd" title="Systemd" id="mwAhM">systemd</a> logo</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAhQ">Between 2013 and 2014, the Debian Technical Committee deliberated on the choice of default <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Init_system" title="Init system" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAhU">init system</a> for the next stable release, evaluating options such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Systemd" title="Systemd" id="mwAhY">systemd</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Upstart_(software)" title="Upstart (software)" id="mwAhc">Upstart</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenRC" title="OpenRC" id="mwAhg">OpenRC</a>.<sup about="#mwt254" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-69" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-69&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-69" id="mwAhk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAho"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhs">[</span>69<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhw">]</span></span></a></sup> The decision, made in February 2014 in favor of systemd,<sup about="#mwt257" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-70" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-70&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-70" id="mwAh0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAh4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAh8">[</span>70<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAiA">]</span></span></a></sup> sparked debate within the community and resulted in the resignation of some developers, including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ian_Jackson_(computer_programmer)" title="Ian Jackson (computer programmer)" id="mwAiE">Ian Jackson</a>.<sup about="#mwt260" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-71" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-71&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-71" id="mwAiI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAiM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAiQ">[</span>71<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAiU">]</span></span></a></sup> Debian 8 "Jessie", released on April 25, 2015, was the first version to adopt systemd as the default.<sup about="#mwt263" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-72" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-72&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-72" id="mwAiY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAic"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAig">[</span>72<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAik">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="24" id="mwAio" aria-labelledby="Microsoft_Azure_endorsement_(2015)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Microsoft_Azure_endorsement_(2015)"><span id="Microsoft_Azure_endorsement_.282015.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Microsoft Azure endorsement (2015)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=24" title="Edit section: Microsoft Azure endorsement (2015)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAis">On December 2, 2015, the Microsoft Azure Team, in collaboration with the consulting and services company Credativ, announced Debian as an endorsed distribution on the Azure Marketplace, allowing customers to provision Debian-based <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virtual_machine" title="Virtual machine" id="mwAiw">virtual machines</a> on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Azure" title="Microsoft Azure" id="mwAi0">Microsoft Azure</a>.<sup about="#mwt266" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-73" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-73&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-73" id="mwAi4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAi8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjA">[</span>73<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="25" id="mwAjI" aria-labelledby="Death_of_Ian_Murdock_(2015)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Death_of_Ian_Murdock_(2015)"><span id="Death_of_Ian_Murdock_.282015.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Death of Ian Murdock (2015)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=25" title="Edit section: Death of Ian Murdock (2015)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAjM">On December 28, 2015, Debian project founder <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ian_Murdock" title="Ian Murdock" id="mwAjQ">Ian Murdock</a> died in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Francisco" title="San Francisco" id="mwAjU">San Francisco</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California" title="California" id="mwAjY">California</a>, at the age of 42. In the days before his death, he had published a series of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twitter" title="Twitter" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAjc">Twitter</a> messages describing a conflict with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Francisco_Police_Department" title="San Francisco Police Department" id="mwAjg">San Francisco Police Department</a>. The cause of death was initially unknown,<sup about="#mwt269" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-74" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-74&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-74" id="mwAjk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAjo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjs">[</span>74<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjw">]</span></span></a></sup> but on July 6, 2016, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CNNMoney" title="CNNMoney" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAj0">CNNMoney</a> reported that it had obtained the autopsy record from the San Francisco medical examiner's office. According to the report, police officers had entered Murdock's home and found him dead, with a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vacuum_cleaner" title="Vacuum cleaner" id="mwAj4">vacuum cleaner</a>'s electrical cord wound tightly around his neck.<sup about="#mwt272" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-75" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-75&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-75" id="mwAj8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAkA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkE">[</span>75<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkI">]</span></span></a></sup> After his death, the Debian project published a memorial in which he was described as the "stalwart proponent of Free Open Source Software, Father, Son, and the 'ian' in Debian."<sup about="#mwt275" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-76" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-76&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-76" id="mwAkM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAkQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkU">[</span>76<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="26" id="mwAkc" aria-labelledby="Recent_history_(2016–present)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Recent_history_(2016–present)"><span id="Recent_history_.282016.E2.80.93present.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Recent history (2016–present)</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=26" title="Edit section: Recent history (2016–present)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="27" id="mwAkg" aria-labelledby="Mozilla_software_renaming_reversal_(2017)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Mozilla_software_renaming_reversal_(2017)"><span id="Mozilla_software_renaming_reversal_.282017.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Mozilla software renaming reversal (2017)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=27" title="Edit section: Mozilla software renaming reversal (2017)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAkk">Starting in 2016 and completed in 2017 with Debian 9 "Stretch",<sup about="#mwt278" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-77" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-77&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-77" id="mwAko"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAks"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkw">[</span>77<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAk0">]</span></span></a></sup> Mozilla Corporation's software was renamed back to its official versions, after the company relicensed the logos under a copyright license compatible with the DFSG and acknowledged that the patches applied by Debian did not compromise the product's quality,<sup about="#mwt281" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-78" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-78&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-78" id="mwAk4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAk8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlA">[</span>78<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlE">]</span></span></a></sup> allowing the project to return to its original visual identity.<sup about="#mwt284" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-79" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-79&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-79" id="mwAlI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAlM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlQ">[</span>79<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt287" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-80" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-80&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-80" id="mwAlY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAlc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlg">[</span>80<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="28" id="mwAlo" aria-labelledby="Windows_Subsystem_for_Linux_availability_(2018)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Windows_Subsystem_for_Linux_availability_(2018)"><span id="Windows_Subsystem_for_Linux_availability_.282018.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Windows Subsystem for Linux availability (2018)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=28" title="Edit section: Windows Subsystem for Linux availability (2018)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAls">In March 2018, Debian became available for download from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Store" title="Microsoft Store" id="mwAlw">Microsoft Store</a> for installation on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_Subsystem_for_Linux" title="Windows Subsystem for Linux" id="mwAl0">Windows Subsystem for Linux</a> (WSL).<sup about="#mwt290" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-81" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-81&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-81" id="mwAl4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAl8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmA">[</span>81<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmE">]</span></span></a></sup> WSL allows developers to install a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux_distribution" title="Linux distribution" id="mwAmI">Linux distribution</a> and use Linux programs on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows" title="Windows" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAmM">Windows</a> without the overhead of a virtual machine or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dual_boot" title="Dual boot" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAmQ">dual boot</a> setup.<sup about="#mwt293" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-82" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-82&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-82" id="mwAmU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAmY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmc">[</span>82<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="29" id="mwAmk" aria-labelledby="&quot;Buster&quot;_and_&quot;Bullseye&quot;_releases_(2019–2021)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="&quot;Buster&quot;_and_&quot;Bullseye&quot;_releases_(2019–2021)"><span id=".22Buster.22_and_.22Bullseye.22_releases_.282019.E2.80.932021.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>"Buster" and "Bullseye" releases (2019–2021)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=29" title="Edit section: &quot;Buster&quot; and &quot;Bullseye&quot; releases (2019–2021)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAmo"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Debian10_Gnome.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAms"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Debian10_Gnome.png" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Debian10_Gnome.png/250px-Debian10_Gnome.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Debian10_Gnome.png/500px-Debian10_Gnome.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1920" data-file-height="1200" data-file-type="bitmap" height="156" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAmw"></a><figcaption id="mwAm0">Debian 10 "Buster", 2019</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAm4">Debian 10 "Buster", released on 6 July 2019,<sup about="#mwt294" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-releases-exact-date_40-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;releases-exact-date&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-releases-exact-date-40" id="mwAm8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAnA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnE">[</span>40<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnI">]</span></span></a></sup> introduced advances in the areas of security and graphical infrastructure. Among the main changes were the addition of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UEFI_Secure_Boot" title="UEFI Secure Boot" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAnM">UEFI Secure Boot</a> support, the enabling of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AppArmor" title="AppArmor" id="mwAnQ">AppArmor</a> by default, and the adoption of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wayland_(protocol)" title="Wayland (protocol)" id="mwAnU">Wayland</a> as the default <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Display_server" title="Display server" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAnY">display server</a> protocol for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GNOME" title="GNOME" id="mwAnc">GNOME</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desktop_environment" title="Desktop environment" id="mwAng">desktop environment</a>. In this release,<sup about="#mwt297" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-buster-released_83-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;buster-released&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-buster-released-83&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-buster-released-83" id="mwAnk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAno"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAns">[</span>83<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnw">]</span></span></a></sup> the project also published a resolution that consolidated <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Systemd" title="Systemd" id="mwAn0">systemd</a> as the system's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Init" title="Init" id="mwAn4">init</a>.<sup about="#mwt300" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-84" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-84&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-84" id="mwAn8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAoA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoE">[</span>84<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoI">]</span></span></a></sup> Debian 11 "Bullseye", released on 14 August 2021, activated systemd's persistent journal functionality by default, introduced driverless scanning support via the sane-escl backend, and became the first release with kernel-level support for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ExFAT" title="ExFAT" id="mwAoM">exFAT</a> filesystem, defaulting to it for mounting exFAT drives.<sup about="#mwt303" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-85" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-85&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-85" id="mwAoQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAoU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoY">[</span>85<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAog"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Debian_12_GRUB,_UEFI_mode.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAok"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Debian_12_GRUB,_UEFI_mode.png" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Debian_12_GRUB%2C_UEFI_mode.png/250px-Debian_12_GRUB%2C_UEFI_mode.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Debian_12_GRUB%2C_UEFI_mode.png/500px-Debian_12_GRUB%2C_UEFI_mode.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="800" data-file-height="600" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAoo"></a><figcaption id="mwAos">Debian 12 "Bookworm" installation menu</figcaption></figure>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="30" id="mwAow" aria-labelledby="XZ_Utils_backdoor_(2024)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="XZ_Utils_backdoor_(2024)"><span id="XZ_Utils_backdoor_.282024.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>XZ Utils backdoor (2024)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=30" title="Edit section: XZ Utils backdoor (2024)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt304" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAo0" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;main&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Main&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;XZ Utils backdoor&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt305" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt304" id="mwAo4">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XZ_Utils_backdoor" title="XZ Utils backdoor">XZ Utils backdoor</a></div>
<p id="mwAo8">On March 29, 2024, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft" title="Microsoft" id="mwApA">Microsoft</a> developer and engineer Andres Freund discovered a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backdoor_(computing)" title="Backdoor (computing)" id="mwApE">backdoor</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XZ_Utils" title="XZ Utils" id="mwApI">XZ Utils</a>, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lossless_compression" title="Lossless compression" id="mwApM">compression</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Library_(computing)" title="Library (computing)" id="mwApQ">library</a>, after noticing unusual <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CPU" title="CPU" class="mw-redirect" id="mwApU">CPU</a> usage and errors generated by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valgrind" title="Valgrind" id="mwApY">Valgrind</a>, a tool for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memory_debugger" title="Memory debugger" id="mwApc">memory</a> debugging, while troubleshooting <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SSH" title="SSH" class="mw-redirect" id="mwApg">SSH</a> performance on Debian "Sid" (<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt306" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwApk" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;unstable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt306" id="mwApo">unstable</span>).<sup about="#mwt316" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-86" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-86&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-86" id="mwAps"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAp0">[</span>86<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAp4">]</span></span></a></sup> The backdoor was later traced to years of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Social_engineering_(security)" title="Social engineering (security)" id="mwAp8">social engineering</a> and code contributions by a contributor using the name Jia Tan. It allowed an attacker with a specific <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Public-key_cryptography" title="Public-key cryptography" id="mwAqA">private key</a> to hijack sshd, the executable responsible for handling SSH connections, and execute arbitrary commands. The vulnerability was assigned the identifier <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_Vulnerabilities_and_Exposures" title="Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures" id="mwAqE">CVE</a>-2024-3094 and given the maximum <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CVSS" title="CVSS" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAqI">CVSS</a> severity score of 10.0.<sup about="#mwt319" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-87" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-87&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-87" id="mwAqM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAqQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqU">[</span>87<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqY">]</span></span></a></sup> The compromised code affected Debian's <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt308" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwAqc" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;testing&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt308" id="mwAqg">testing</span>, <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt310" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwAqk" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;unstable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt310" id="mwAqo">unstable</span>, and <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt312" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwAqs" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;experimental&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt312" id="mwAqw">experimental</span> suites, among other <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux_distributions" title="Linux distributions" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAq0">Linux distributions</a>.<sup about="#mwt322" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-88" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-88&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-88" id="mwAq4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAq8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArA">[</span>88<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt325" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-89" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-89&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-89" id="mwArI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArQ">[</span>89<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="31" id="mwArY" aria-labelledby="&quot;Bookworm&quot;_and_&quot;Trixie&quot;_releases_(2023–2025)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="&quot;Bookworm&quot;_and_&quot;Trixie&quot;_releases_(2023–2025)"><span id=".22Bookworm.22_and_.22Trixie.22_releases_.282023.E2.80.932025.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>"Bookworm" and "Trixie" releases (2023–2025)</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=31" title="Edit section: &quot;Bookworm&quot; and &quot;Trixie&quot; releases (2023–2025)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwArc">Debian 12 "Bookworm", released on June 10, 2023, was the first stable release to include non-free firmware packages by default in the installer when the system detects that they are necessary.<sup about="#mwt328" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-90" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-90&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-90" id="mwArg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAro">[</span>90<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArs">]</span></span></a></sup> This followed the 2022 General Resolution on non-free firmware, which decided to amend the Debian Social Contract to permit the inclusion of firmware that is otherwise not part of the system, in order to enable the use of Debian on hardware that requires it.<sup about="#mwt331" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-91" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-91&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-91" id="mwArw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAr0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAr4">[</span>91<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAr8">]</span></span></a></sup> Debian 13 "Trixie", released on August 9, 2025, added support for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RISC-V" title="RISC-V" id="mwAsA">riscv64</a> architecture and dropped support for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I386" title="I386" id="mwAsE">i386</a> as a regular architecture, meaning there is no official <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux_kernel" title="Linux kernel" id="mwAsI">kernel</a> or Debian-Installer for it.<sup about="#mwt332" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-trixie-released_19-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;trixie-released&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-trixie-released-19" id="mwAsM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAsQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsU">[</span>19<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section></section><section data-mw-section-id="32" id="mwAsc" aria-labelledby="Distribution"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Distribution">Distribution</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=32" title="Edit section: Distribution"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAsg"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Debian10-CD-Cover.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAsk"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Debian10-CD-Cover.png" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Debian10-CD-Cover.png/250px-Debian10-CD-Cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Debian10-CD-Cover.png/500px-Debian10-CD-Cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="775" data-file-height="519" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAso"></a><figcaption id="mwAss">Debian 10 "Buster" box cover</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAsw">Debian provides its entire distribution free of charge. The project does not manufacture <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CD" title="CD" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAs0">CDs</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DVD" title="DVD" id="mwAs4">DVDs</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blu-ray" title="Blu-ray" id="mwAs8">Blu-ray discs</a>, or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/USB_flash_drive" title="USB flash drive" id="mwAtA">USB flash drives</a>, relying instead on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Third-party_source" title="Third-party source" id="mwAtE">third-party</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vendor" title="Vendor" id="mwAtI">vendors</a> for that purpose. To help vendors produce disks of consistent quality, Debian supplies official <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Optical_disc_image" title="Optical disc image" id="mwAtM">images</a> that have been fully tested by its testing team.<sup about="#mwt335" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-92" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-92&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-92" id="mwAtQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAtU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtY">[</span>92<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAtg">The Debian distribution is <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirror_site" title="Mirror site" id="mwAtk">mirrored</a> on hundreds of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Server_(computing)" title="Server (computing)" id="mwAto">servers</a> worldwide. In addition to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTTP" title="HTTP" id="mwAts">HTTP</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FTP" title="FTP" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAtw">FTP</a>, images can be obtained through other download methods.<sup about="#mwt340" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-debian-mirrors-list_93-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;debian-mirrors-list&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-debian-mirrors-list-93&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-debian-mirrors-list-93" id="mwAt0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAt4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAt8">[</span>93<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuA">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jigdo" title="Jigdo" id="mwAuE">Jigsaw</a> Download, commonly known as jigdo, is a bandwidth friendly method of distributing Debian USB, CD, and DVD images.<sup about="#mwt343" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-94" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-94&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-94" id="mwAuI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAuM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuQ">[</span>94<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuU">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BitTorrent" title="BitTorrent" id="mwAuY">BitTorrent</a>, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peer-to-peer" title="Peer-to-peer" id="mwAuc">peer-to-peer</a> download system optimised for large numbers of simultaneous downloaders, is also supported, and requires the use of a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BitTorrent_client" title="BitTorrent client" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAug">BitTorrent client</a>. The Debian distribution itself includes such tools, among them <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt336" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwAuk" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;aria2&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt336" id="mwAuo">aria2</span>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transmission_(BitTorrent_client)" title="Transmission (BitTorrent client)" id="mwAus">Transmission</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/QBittorrent" title="QBittorrent" id="mwAuw">qBittorrent</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KTorrent" title="KTorrent" id="mwAu0">KTorrent</a>, while users of other operating systems, such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Windows" title="Microsoft Windows" id="mwAu4">Windows</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MacOS" title="MacOS" id="mwAu8">macOS</a>, can use clients including qBittorrent and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BitTorrent_(software)" title="BitTorrent (software)" id="mwAvA">BitTorrent</a>.<sup about="#mwt346" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-95" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-95&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-95" id="mwAvE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAvI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvM">[</span>95<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAvU">Users may purchase a set of CDs, DVDs, or a USB stick from a vendor, or they may download the installation images from a Debian mirror and create their own installation media, provided they have a sufficiently fast network connection along with a CD or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DVD_burner" title="DVD burner" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAvY">DVD burner</a> or a USB flash drive. Once such installation media has been created, and assuming it is bootable on the target machine, the installation process can proceed directly to booting the installation system.<sup about="#mwt349" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-96" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-96&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-96" id="mwAvc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAvg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvk">[</span>96<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="33" id="mwAvs" aria-labelledby="Image_sizes"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Image_sizes">Image sizes</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=33" title="Edit section: Image sizes"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAvw">Debian offers its images in several sizes to accommodate different types of media. CD images are up to 700 megabytes in size and are suitable for writing to standard <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CD-R" title="CD-R" id="mwAv0">CD-R</a> or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CD-RW" title="CD-RW" id="mwAv4">CD-RW</a> media. DVD images are up to 4.7 gigabytes in size and are suitable for writing to standard <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DVD-R" title="DVD-R" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAv8">DVD-R</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DVD+R" title="DVD+R" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAwA">DVD+R</a>, and similar media.<sup about="#mwt352" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-97" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-97&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-97" id="mwAwE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAwI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwM">[</span>97<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="34" id="mwAwU" aria-labelledby="USB_installation_media"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="USB_installation_media">USB installation media</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=34" title="Edit section: USB installation media"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAwY">Debian installation images are also distributed as smaller image files suitable for USB flash drives and similar <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Removable_media" title="Removable media" id="mwAwc">removable devices</a>. Because Debian CD and DVD images are created in an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hybrid_disc" title="Hybrid disc" id="mwAwg">isohybrid</a> format, they can boot from either <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Optical_disc_drive" title="Optical disc drive" id="mwAwk">optical disc drives</a> or USB drives. As a result, the simplest method of preparing a USB memory stick is to download a CD or DVD image that fits on the device and write it directly to the stick, an action that erases any existing data on the device.<sup about="#mwt355" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-98" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-98&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-98" id="mwAwo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAws"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAww">[</span>98<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAw0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="35" id="mwAw4" aria-labelledby="Network_installation"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Network_installation">Network installation</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=35" title="Edit section: Network installation"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAw8">A network installation, or "netinst", image is a single CD or DVD that allows installation of the entire operating system. It contains only the minimal software required to install the base system, and the remaining packages are fetched over the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet" title="Internet" id="mwAxA">Internet</a> during installation.<sup about="#mwt358" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-99" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-99&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-99" id="mwAxE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAxI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxM">[</span>99<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxQ">]</span></span></a></sup> In later releases, such as "Trixie", the netinst image includes the components needed to run the Debian Installer along with the base packages required for a minimal system, while users who prefer not to rely on a network connection during installation can instead use a full DVD image.<sup about="#mwt361" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-100" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-100&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-100" id="mwAxU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAxY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxc">[</span>100<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="36" id="mwAxk" aria-labelledby="Live_images"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Live_images">Live images</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=36" title="Edit section: Live images"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt362" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAxo" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;See also&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:See_also&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Comparison of X Window System desktop environments&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt363" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt362" id="mwAxs">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comparison_of_X_Window_System_desktop_environments" title="Comparison of X Window System desktop environments">Comparison of X Window System desktop environments</a></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAxw"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Debian_13.0.0_KDE_default_desktop_-_English.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAx0"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Debian_13.0.0_KDE_default_desktop_-_English.png" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Debian_13.0.0_KDE_default_desktop_-_English.png/250px-Debian_13.0.0_KDE_default_desktop_-_English.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Debian_13.0.0_KDE_default_desktop_-_English.png/500px-Debian_13.0.0_KDE_default_desktop_-_English.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1454" data-file-height="991" data-file-type="bitmap" height="170" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAx4"></a><figcaption id="mwAx8">Debian 13 "Trixie" running <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KDE_Plasma_6" title="KDE Plasma 6" id="mwAyA">KDE Plasma 6</a> in a live environment</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAyE">In addition to the standard installation images, Debian offers <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Live_USB" title="Live USB" id="mwAyI">live images</a>. A live image contains a complete Debian system that can be booted without modifying any files on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computer_data_storage" title="Computer data storage" id="mwAyM">computer's storage</a>, and it also allows Debian to be installed directly from the contents of the image. Live images are offered for the <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt364" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwAyQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;stable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt364" id="mwAyU">stable</span> and <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt366" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwAyY" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;testing&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt366" id="mwAyc">testing</span> suites and are available in several flavors,<sup about="#mwt370" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-101" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-101&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-101" id="mwAyg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAyk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyo">[</span>101<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAys">]</span></span></a></sup> each offering a different <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desktop_environment" title="Desktop environment" id="mwAyw">desktop environment</a>, including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GNOME" title="GNOME" id="mwAy0">GNOME</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KDE_Plasma" title="KDE Plasma" id="mwAy4">KDE Plasma</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xfce" title="Xfce" id="mwAy8">Xfce</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LXQt" title="LXQt" id="mwAzA">LXQt</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LXDE" title="LXDE" id="mwAzE">LXDE</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinnamon_(desktop_environment)" title="Cinnamon (desktop environment)" id="mwAzI">Cinnamon</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MATE_(desktop_environment)" title="MATE (desktop environment)" id="mwAzM">MATE</a>.<sup about="#mwt373" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-102" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-102&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-102" id="mwAzQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAzU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzY">[</span>102<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzc">]</span></span></a></sup> Live images are provided only for the amd64 architecture. They include the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calamares_(software)" title="Calamares (software)" id="mwAzg">Calamares Installer</a>, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux_distribution" title="Linux distribution" id="mwAzk">distribution</a>-independent installer framework intended to be easy for end users to operate. The images do not contain a complete set of language support packages, so users who require <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Input_method" title="Input method" id="mwAzo">input methods</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Font" title="Font" id="mwAzs">fonts</a>, or other supplemental packages for their language must install these separately afterward. Live images are suitable for users who wish to try a Debian system and then install it from the same media, and they can be written to a USB flash drive or to DVD-R(W) media.<sup about="#mwt376" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-103" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-103&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-103" id="mwAzw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAz0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAz4">[</span>103<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAz8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="37" id="mwA0A" aria-labelledby="Cloud_images"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Cloud_images">Cloud images</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=37" title="Edit section: Cloud images"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwA0E">Debian provides <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virtual_machine" title="Virtual machine" id="mwA0I">virtual machine</a> images that can be provisioned through service calls, configured and manipulated with manual or automated tools, and terminated when no longer needed. It supports several cloud-oriented use cases, including running as a guest operating system on various services, running the infrastructure that hosts a private cloud, and running as a client that interacts with cloud services through <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/API" title="API" id="mwA0M">APIs</a> or other network services.</p>

<p id="mwA0Q">Debian publishes official virtual machine images for the following cloud environments and marketplaces:</p>
<ul id="mwA0U"><li id="mwA0Y"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_Web_Services" title="Amazon Web Services" id="mwA0c">Amazon Web Services</a>, through the AWS Marketplace</li>
<li id="mwA0g"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Azure" title="Microsoft Azure" id="mwA0k">Microsoft Azure</a>, through the Azure Marketplace</li>
<li id="mwA0o"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenStack" title="OpenStack" id="mwA0s">OpenStack</a>, using generic images for the "Trixie" and "Bookworm" releases</li></ul>

<p id="mwA0w">Unofficial or third party images are also available. For example, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google" title="Google" id="mwA00">Google</a> publishes images for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google_Compute_Engine" title="Google Compute Engine" id="mwA04">Google Compute Engine</a> that include software and APT repositories not included in Debian.<sup about="#mwt379" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-104" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-104&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-104" id="mwA08"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA1A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA1E">[</span>104<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA1I">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="38" id="mwA1M" aria-labelledby="Network_booting"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Network_booting">Network booting</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=38" title="Edit section: Network booting"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwA1Q">Installation over a local network is also supported through <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Network_booting" title="Network booting" id="mwA1U">network booting</a>. In this method, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TFTP" title="TFTP" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA1Y">TFTP</a> server and a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DHCP" title="DHCP" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA1c">DHCP</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BOOTP" title="BOOTP" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA1g">BOOTP</a>, or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RARP" title="RARP" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA1k">RARP</a> server are configured to serve installation media to client machines on the network. If a client machine's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BIOS" title="BIOS" id="mwA1o">BIOS</a> supports the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Preboot_Execution_Environment" title="Preboot Execution Environment" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA1s">Preboot Execution Environment</a> (PXE), it can boot the Debian installation system over the network using PXE and TFTP, after which the remainder of the installation proceeds over the network.<sup about="#mwt382" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-105" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-105&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-105" id="mwA1w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA10"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA14">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA18">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="39" id="mwA2A" aria-labelledby="Verifying_downloads"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Verifying_downloads">Verifying downloads</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=39" title="Edit section: Verifying downloads"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwA2E">To verify the integrity and authenticity of downloaded images, official Debian installation and live images are accompanied by signed <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File_verification" title="File verification" id="mwA2I">checksum files</a>, located alongside the images in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Directory_(computing)" title="Directory (computing)" id="mwA2M">directories</a> such as <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt383" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA2Q" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;iso-cd&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt383" id="mwA2U">iso-cd</span>, <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt385" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA2Y" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;jigdo-dvd&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt385" id="mwA2c">jigdo-dvd</span>, and <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt387" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA2g" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;iso-hybrid&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt387" id="mwA2k">iso-hybrid</span>. The checksums allow users to confirm that an image was not <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_corruption" title="Data corruption" id="mwA2o">corrupted</a> during download, while the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_signatures" title="Digital signatures" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA2s">digital signatures</a> on the checksum files allow users to confirm that the image was created and released by Debian and has not been tampered with.<sup about="#mwt391" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-106" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-106&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-106" id="mwA2w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA20"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA24">[</span>106<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA28">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="40" id="mwA3A" aria-labelledby="Packages"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Packages">Packages</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=40" title="Edit section: Packages"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwA3E">Debian <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_build" title="Software build" id="mwA3I">builds</a> distributions of pre-<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compiler" title="Compiler" id="mwA3M">compiled</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Free_Software" title="Free Software" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA3Q">freely licensed</a> binary <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Package_format" title="Package format" id="mwA3U">packages</a> and distributes them through its archive.<sup about="#mwt394" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-107" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-107&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-107" id="mwA3Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA3c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3g">[</span>107<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3k">]</span></span></a></sup> Packages generally contain all of the files necessary to implement a set of related commands or features. There are two types of Debian packages: binary packages and source packages.</p>

<p id="mwA3o">Binary packages contain <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Executable" title="Executable" id="mwA3s">executables</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Configuration_file" title="Configuration file" id="mwA3w">configuration files</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Man_pages" title="Man pages" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA30">man pages</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Copyright" title="Copyright" id="mwA34">copyright</a> information, and other documentation. These packages are distributed in a Debian-specific archive format and are typically identified by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File_extension" title="File extension" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA38">file extension</a> "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deb_(file_format)" title="Deb (file format)" id="mwA4A">.deb</a>". Binary packages can be unpacked using the Debian utility <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dpkg" title="Dpkg" id="mwA4E">dpkg</a>, or through a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Front_end_and_back_end" title="Front end and back end" id="mwA4I">front end</a> such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Advanced_Package_Tool" title="Advanced Package Tool" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA4M">apt</a>.</p>

<p id="mwA4Q">Source packages consist of a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debian_build_toolchain#Source_packages" title="Debian build toolchain" id="mwA4U">.dsc</a> file describing the source package, including the names of associated files, an <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt395" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA4Y" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;.orig.tar.gz&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt395" id="mwA4c">.orig.tar.gz</span> file containing the original, unmodified source in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gzip" title="Gzip" id="mwA4g">gzip</a> compressed <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tar" title="Tar" id="mwA4k">tar</a> format, and, typically, a <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt397" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA4o" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;.debian.tar.xz&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt397" id="mwA4s">.debian.tar.xz</span> file containing the Debian specific changes to the original source. The utility <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt399" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA4w" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;dpkg-source&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt399" id="mwA40">dpkg-source</span> is used to pack and unpack Debian source archives. The program <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt401" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA44" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;apt-get&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt401" id="mwA48">apt-get</span> can also be used as a front end for <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt403" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA5A" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;dpkg-source&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt403" id="mwA5E">dpkg-source</span>.</p>

<p id="mwA5I">Installation of software through the package system relies on dependencies, which are defined by package maintainers and documented in the control file associated with each package. For example, the package containing the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GNU_Compiler_Collection" title="GNU Compiler Collection" id="mwA5M">GNU Compiler Collection</a> (<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt405" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA5Q" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;gcc&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt405" id="mwA5U">gcc</span>) depends on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Binutils" title="Binutils" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA5Y">binutils</a> package, which includes the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linker_(computing)" title="Linker (computing)" id="mwA5c">linker</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assembly_language#Assembler" title="Assembly language" id="mwA5g">assembler</a>. If a user attempts to install <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt407" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA5k" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;gcc&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt407" id="mwA5o">gcc</span> without first installing <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt409" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA5s" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;binutils&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt409" id="mwA5w">binutils</span>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Package_management_system" title="Package management system" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA50">package management system</a> (<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt411" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA54" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;dpkg&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt411" id="mwA58">dpkg</span>) reports an error indicating that <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt413" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA6A" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;binutils&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt413" id="mwA6E">binutils</span> is also required and halts installation of <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt415" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA6I" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;gcc&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt415" id="mwA6M">gcc</span>.</p>

<p id="mwA6Q">Debian's packaging tools support a range of functions, including manipulating and managing packages or their components, administering local overrides of files within them, assisting developers in building package archives, and helping users install those residing on a remote archive site.<sup about="#mwt419" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-108" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-108&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-108" id="mwA6U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA6Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6c">[</span>108<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6g">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwA6k"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Debian_13_Aptitude_Package_Details.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwA6o"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Debian_13_Aptitude_Package_Details.png" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Debian_13_Aptitude_Package_Details.png/250px-Debian_13_Aptitude_Package_Details.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Debian_13_Aptitude_Package_Details.png/500px-Debian_13_Aptitude_Package_Details.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="732" data-file-height="496" data-file-type="bitmap" height="169" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwA6s"></a><figcaption id="mwA6w"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aptitude_(software)" title="Aptitude (software)" id="mwA60">aptitude</a> showing <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KornShell" title="KornShell" id="mwA64">AT&amp;T KornShell</a> package details</figcaption></figure> <figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwA68"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Debian-aptitude.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwA7A"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Debian-aptitude.png" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Debian-aptitude.png/250px-Debian-aptitude.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Debian-aptitude.png/500px-Debian-aptitude.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="661" data-file-height="482" data-file-type="bitmap" height="182" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwA7E"></a><figcaption id="mwA7I">Package installed with <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt420" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA7M" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;aptitude&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt420" id="mwA7Q">aptitude</span></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwA7U">Multiple tools are used to manage Debian packages, ranging from graphical or text-based interfaces to lower-level utilities used for direct package installation. All of them depend on these lower-level utilities to function properly. For example, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aptitude" title="Aptitude" id="mwA7Y">aptitude</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Synaptic_(software)" title="Synaptic (software)" id="mwA7c">synaptic</a> rely on <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt422" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA7g" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;apt&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt422" id="mwA7k">apt</span>, which in turn relies on <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt424" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA7o" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;dpkg&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt424" id="mwA7s">dpkg</span> to manage packages on the system.<sup about="#mwt428" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-109" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-109&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-109" id="mwA7w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA70"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA74">[</span>109<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA78">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="41" id="mwA8A" aria-labelledby="Repositories"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Repositories">Repositories</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=41" title="Edit section: Repositories"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwA8E">A Debian repository is a set of Debian binary or source packages organized in a special directory tree, with various infrastructure files (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Checksum" title="Checksum" id="mwA8I">checksums</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Index_mapping" title="Index mapping" id="mwA8M">indices</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_signature" title="Digital signature" id="mwA8Q">signatures</a>, descriptions, translations, and so on) added. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Client_(computing)" title="Client (computing)" id="mwA8U">Client computers</a> can connect to the repository to download and install packages using an APT-based package management tool.</p>

<p id="mwA8Y">A Debian repository contains several releases. Debian releases are named after characters from the <i id="mwA8c"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toy_Story" title="Toy Story" id="mwA8g">Toy Story</a></i> franchise. The codenames have aliases according to their maturity stage, known as suites (<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt429" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA8k" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;stable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt429" id="mwA8o">stable</span>, <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt431" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA8s" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;oldstable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt431" id="mwA8w">oldstable</span>, <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt433" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA80" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;testing&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt433" id="mwA84">testing</span>, and <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt435" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA88" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;unstable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt435" id="mwA9A">unstable</span>). A release is divided into several components. In Debian these are named <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt437" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA9E" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;main&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt437" id="mwA9I">main</span>, <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt439" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA9M" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;non-free-firmware&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt439" id="mwA9Q">non-free-firmware</span>, <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt441" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA9U" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;contrib&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt441" id="mwA9Y">contrib</span>, and <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt443" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA9c" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;non-free&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt443" id="mwA9g">non-free</span>, and they indicate the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/License" title="License" id="mwA9k">licensing</a> terms of the software they contain. A release also has packages for various architectures, as well as sources and architecture-independent packages.</p>

<p id="mwA9o">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Root_directory" title="Root directory" id="mwA9s">root directory</a> of a repository has a directory called <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt445" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA9w" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;dists&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt445" id="mwA90">dists</span>, which in turn has a directory for each release and suite. The suite directory is usually a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symlink" title="Symlink" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA94">symlink</a> to the release directory, but this is not visible when browsing. Each release subdirectory contains a cryptographically signed <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt447" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA98" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Release&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt447" id="mwA-A">Release</span> file and a directory for each component. Inside these are directories for the different architectures, named <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt449" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA-E" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;binary-&lt;arch&gt;&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt449" id="mwA-I">binary-&lt;arch&gt;</span> and <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt451" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA-M" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;source&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt451" id="mwA-Q">source</span>. Within these are files named <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt453" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA-U" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Packages&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt453" id="mwA-Y">Packages</span>, which are text files containing the metadata of packages. The actual packages are stored elsewhere.</p>

<p id="mwA-c">The packages themselves are located below <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt455" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA-g" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;pool&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt455" id="mwA-k">pool</span> in the root directory of the repository. Below <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt457" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA-o" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;pool&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt457" id="mwA-s">pool</span> there are again directories for all the components, and within these are directories named <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt459" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA-w" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt459" id="mwA-0">0</span> through <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt461" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA-4" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;9&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt461" id="mwA-8">9</span>, <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt463" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA_A" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;a&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt463" id="mwA_E">a</span> through <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt465" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA_I" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;z&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt465" id="mwA_M">z</span>, and <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt467" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA_Q" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;liba&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt467" id="mwA_U">liba</span> through <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt469" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA_Y" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;libz&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt469" id="mwA_c">libz</span>. These contain directories named after the software package they belong to, and these directories finally contain the actual packages, that is, the <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt471" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA_g" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;.deb&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt471" id="mwA_k">.deb</span> files. The name is not necessarily the name of the package itself. For example, the package <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt473" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA_o" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;bsdutils&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt473" id="mwA_s">bsdutils</span> resides in the <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt475" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA_w" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;pool/main/u/util-linux&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt475" id="mwA_0">pool/main/u/util-linux</span> directory, named after the source package from which it is generated. A single <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Upstream_(software_development)" title="Upstream (software development)" id="mwA_4">upstream</a> source may generate several binary packages, and all of them end up in the same subdirectory below <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt477" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwA_8" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;pool&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt477" id="mwBAA">pool</span>. The additional single-letter directories are a way to avoid having too many entries in a single directory, which is a known performance problem for many <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File_system" title="File system" id="mwBAE">file systems</a>.</p>

<p id="mwBAI">In the leaf directories below <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt479" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBAM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;pool&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt479" id="mwBAQ">pool</span> there are usually several versions of a package, and information about which releases each version belongs to resides solely in the indices. This way, the same version of a package can belong to several releases while using disk space only once, without resorting to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hard_link" title="Hard link" id="mwBAU">hard links</a> or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symbolic_link" title="Symbolic link" id="mwBAY">symbolic links</a>, which allows mirroring to remain simple and to work even with systems that lack these concepts.<sup about="#mwt483" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-110" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-110&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-110" id="mwBAc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBAg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBAk">[</span>110<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBAo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="42" id="mwBAs" aria-labelledby="Components"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Components">Components</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=42" title="Edit section: Components"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwBAw">A repository may be divided into one or more of these components, and users might not choose to use all of them. Debian repositories generally include the following components:</p>

<ul id="mwBA0"><li id="mwBA4"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt484" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBA8" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;main&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt484" id="mwBBA">main</span>: Packages that comply with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debian_Free_Software_Guidelines" title="Debian Free Software Guidelines" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBBE">Debian Free Software Guidelines</a> (DFSG) and depend only on other DFSG-compliant packages. Only these packages are considered part of Debian proper.</li>
<li id="mwBBI"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt486" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBBM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;contrib&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt486" id="mwBBQ">contrib</span>: DFSG-compliant packages that depend on packages that do not comply with the DFSG.</li>
<li id="mwBBU"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt488" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBBY" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;non-free&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt488" id="mwBBc">non-free</span>: Packages that do not comply with the DFSG but are considered important enough to be made available anyway. One example is widely used fonts with unusual licensing requirements.</li>
<li id="mwBBg"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt490" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBBk" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;non-free-firmware&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt490" id="mwBBo">non-free-firmware</span>: Non-DFSG-compliant <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firmware" title="Firmware" id="mwBBs">firmware</a> packages, such as those for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Network_cards" title="Network cards" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBBw">network cards</a>. These have been included by default since the release of Debian 12 "Bookworm".<sup about="#mwt494" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-111" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-111&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-111" id="mwBB0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBB4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBB8">[</span>111<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBCA">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section></section></section><section data-mw-section-id="43" id="mwBCE" aria-labelledby="Branches"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Branches">Branches</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=43" title="Edit section: Branches"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwBCI">Three <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Branching_(version_control)" title="Branching (version control)" id="mwBCM">branches</a> of Debian (also called <i id="mwBCQ">releases</i>, <i id="mwBCU">distributions</i> or <i id="mwBCY">suites</i>) are regularly maintained:<sup about="#mwt495" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-releases-exact-date_40-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;releases-exact-date&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-releases-exact-date-40" id="mwBCc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBCg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBCk">[</span>40<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBCo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<ul id="mwBCs"><li id="mwBCw"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt496" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBC0" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;stable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt496" id="mwBC4">stable</span> is the current release and targets stable and well-tested software needs.<sup about="#mwt506" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-112" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-112&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-112" id="mwBC8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBDA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBDE">[</span>112<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBDI">]</span></span></a></sup> <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt498" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBDM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;stable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt498" id="mwBDQ">stable</span> is made by freezing <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt500" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBDU" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;testing&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt500" id="mwBDY">testing</span> for a few months to fix bugs and remove packages with too many bugs; then the resulting system is released as <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt502" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBDc" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;stable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt502" id="mwBDg">stable</span>. It is updated only for major security or usability fixes. This branch has an optional <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backporting" title="Backporting" id="mwBDk">backporting</a> service that provides more recent versions of some software.<sup about="#mwt509" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-113" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-113&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-113" id="mwBDo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBDs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBDw">[</span>113<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBD0">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBD4"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt510" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBD8" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;testing&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt510" id="mwBEA">testing</span> is the preview branch that eventually becomes the next major release. The packages included in this branch have had some testing in <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt512" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBEE" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;unstable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt512" id="mwBEI">unstable</span> but may not be ready for release yet. It contains newer packages than <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt514" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBEM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;stable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt514" id="mwBEQ">stable</span> but older than <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt516" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBEU" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;unstable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt516" id="mwBEY">unstable</span>. This branch is updated continually until it is frozen.</li>
<li id="mwBEc"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt518" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBEg" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;unstable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt518" id="mwBEk">unstable</span>, always codenamed "Sid", is the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trunk_(software)" title="Trunk (software)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBEo">trunk</a>. Packages are accepted without checking the distribution as a whole. This branch is usually run by software developers who participate in a project and need the latest libraries available, and by those who prefer <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bleeding_edge_technology" title="Bleeding edge technology" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBEs">bleeding-edge</a> software.<sup about="#mwt520" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-releases-exact-date_40-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;releases-exact-date&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-releases-exact-date-40" id="mwBEw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBE0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBE4">[</span>40<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBE8">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

<p id="mwBFA">Other branches in Debian:</p>
<ul id="mwBFE"><li id="mwBFI"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt521" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBFM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;oldstable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt521" id="mwBFQ">oldstable</span> is the prior <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt523" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBFU" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;stable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt523" id="mwBFY">stable</span> release. It is supported by the Debian Security Team for one year after a new <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt525" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBFc" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;stable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt525" id="mwBFg">stable</span> is released, and then for another two years through the Long Term Support project.<sup about="#mwt531" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-security-faq_114-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;security-faq&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-security-faq-114&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-security-faq-114" id="mwBFk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBFo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBFs">[</span>114<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBFw">]</span></span></a></sup> Eventually, <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt527" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBF0" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;oldstable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt527" id="mwBF4">oldstable</span> is moved to a repository for archived releases.</li>
<li id="mwBF8"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt532" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBGA" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;experimental&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt532" id="mwBGE">experimental</span> is a temporary staging area of highly experimental software that is likely to break the system. It is not a full distribution and missing dependencies are commonly found in <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt534" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBGI" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;unstable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt534" id="mwBGM">unstable</span>, where new software without the damage risk is normally uploaded.<sup about="#mwt538" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-distributions_115-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;distributions&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-distributions-115&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-distributions-115" id="mwBGQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBGU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBGY">[</span>115<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBGc">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

<p id="mwBGg">The <i id="mwBGk">snapshot</i> archive provides older versions of the branches. They may be used to install a specific older version of some software.<sup about="#mwt541" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-116" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-116&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-116" id="mwBGo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBGs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBGw">[</span>116<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBG0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="44" id="mwBG4" aria-labelledby="Numbering_scheme"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Numbering_scheme">Numbering scheme</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=44" title="Edit section: Numbering scheme"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwBG8"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt542" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBHA" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;stable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt542" id="mwBHE">stable</span> and <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt544" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBHI" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;oldstable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt544" id="mwBHM">oldstable</span> get minor updates, called <i id="mwBHQ">point releases</i>. The numbering scheme for the point releases up to Debian 4.0 "Etch" was to include the letter <i id="mwBHU">r</i> (for <i id="mwBHY">revision</i>)<sup about="#mwt546" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEHertzog2013Section_1.6_117-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEHertzog2013Section 1.6&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEHertzog2013Section_1.6-117&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Hertzog&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2013&quot;},&quot;loc&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Section 1.6&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEHertzog2013Section_1.6-117" id="mwBHc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBHg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBHk">[</span>117<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBHo">]</span></span></a></sup> after the main version number and then the number of the point release; for example, the latest point release of version 4.0 is 4.0r9.<sup about="#mwt551" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-118" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-118&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-118" id="mwBHs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBHw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBH0">[</span>118<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBH4">]</span></span></a></sup> This scheme was chosen because a new dotted version would make the old one look obsolete and vendors would have trouble selling their CDs.<sup about="#mwt554" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-119" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-119&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-119" id="mwBH8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBIA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBIE">[</span>119<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBII">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBIM">From Debian 5.0 "Lenny", the numbering scheme of point releases was changed, conforming to the GNU version numbering standard;<sup about="#mwt557" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-120" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-120&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-120" id="mwBIQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBIU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBIY">[</span>120<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBIc">]</span></span></a></sup> the first point release of Debian 5.0 was 5.0.1 instead of 5.0r1.<sup about="#mwt560" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-121" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-121&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-121" id="mwBIg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBIk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBIo">[</span>121<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBIs">]</span></span></a></sup> The numbering scheme was once again changed for the first Debian 7 "Wheezy" update, which was version 7.1.<sup about="#mwt563" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-122" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-122&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-122" id="mwBIw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBI0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBI4">[</span>122<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBI8">]</span></span></a></sup> The <i id="mwBJA">r</i> scheme is no longer in use, but point release announcements include a note about not throwing away old installation media.<sup about="#mwt566" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-123" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-123&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-123" id="mwBJE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBJI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBJM">[</span>123<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBJQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="45" id="mwBJU" aria-labelledby="Hardware"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Hardware">Hardware</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=45" title="Edit section: Hardware"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwBJY">Hardware requirements are at least those of the kernel and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GNU" title="GNU" id="mwBJc">GNU</a> toolsets.<sup about="#mwt569" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-supported-hardware_124-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;supported-hardware&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-supported-hardware-124&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-supported-hardware-124" id="mwBJg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBJk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBJo">[</span>124<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBJs">]</span></span></a></sup> Debian's recommended system requirements depend on the level of installation, which corresponds to increased numbers of installed components:</p>

<table class="wikitable" style="text-align:center;" id="mwBJw">
<tbody id="mwBJ0"><tr id="mwBJ4">
<th id="mwBJ8">Type</th>
<th id="mwBKA">Minimum <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Random-access_memory" title="Random-access memory" id="mwBKE">RAM</a> size</th>
<th id="mwBKI">Recommended RAM size</th>
<th id="mwBKM">Minimum processor <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clock_rate" title="Clock rate" id="mwBKQ">clock speed</a> (IA-32)</th>
<th id="mwBKU">Hard-drive capacity</th></tr>
<tr id="mwBKY">
<td id="mwBKc">Non-desktop</td>
<td id="mwBKg">512<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Megabyte" title="Megabyte" id="mwBKk">MB</a></td>
<td id="mwBKo">1<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gigabyte" title="Gigabyte" id="mwBKs">GB</a></td>
<td id="mwBKw"></td>
<td id="mwBK0">4GB</td></tr>
<tr id="mwBK4">
<td id="mwBK8">Desktop</td>
<td id="mwBLA">1GB</td>
<td id="mwBLE">2GB</td>
<td id="mwBLI">1GHz</td>
<td id="mwBLM">10GB</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<p id="mwBLQ">The real minimum memory requirements depend on the architecture and may be much less than the numbers listed in this table. It is possible to install Debian with 170MB of RAM for x86-64; the installer will run in low memory mode and it is recommended to create a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paging" title="Paging" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBLU">swap partition</a>.<sup about="#mwt572" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-125" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-125&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-125" id="mwBLY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBLc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLg">[</span>125<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLk">]</span></span></a></sup> The installer for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Z/Architecture" title="Z/Architecture" id="mwBLo">z/Architecture</a> requires about 20MB of RAM, but relies on network hardware.<sup about="#mwt575" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-126" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-126&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-126" id="mwBLs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBLw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBL0">[</span>126<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBL4">]</span></span></a></sup> Similarly, disk space requirements, which depend on the packages to be installed, can be reduced by manually selecting the packages needed.</p>

<p id="mwBL8">It is possible to run <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graphical_user_interface" title="Graphical user interface" id="mwBMA">graphical user interfaces</a> on older or low-end systems. However, installing <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Window_manager" title="Window manager" id="mwBME">window managers</a> instead of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desktop_environment" title="Desktop environment" id="mwBMI">desktop environments</a> is recommended, as desktop environments use more resources. Requirements for individual software vary widely and must be considered, with those of the base operating environment.<sup about="#mwt578" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-hardware-requeriments_127-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;hardware-requeriments&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-hardware-requeriments-127&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-hardware-requeriments-127" id="mwBMM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBMQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBMU">[</span>127<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBMY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="46" id="mwBMc" aria-labelledby="Architectures"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Architectures">Architectures</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=46" title="Edit section: Architectures"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwBMg"><span about="#mwt579" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBMk" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;As of&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:As_of&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2025&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;8&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;9&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">As of 9</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt579">&nbsp;</span><span about="#mwt579">August</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt579">&nbsp;</span><span about="#mwt579">2025</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt579"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt579"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_August_2025" about="#mwt579"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt579" id="mwBMo">, the "Trixie" release, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instruction_set_architecture" title="Instruction set architecture" id="mwBMs">instruction set architecture</a> officially supported are:</p>
<ul id="mwBMw"><li id="mwBM0">amd64: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X86-64" title="X86-64" id="mwBM4">x86-64</a> 64-bit</li>
<li id="mwBM8">arm64: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ARMv8" title="ARMv8" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBNA">ARMv8</a> 64-bit</li>
<li id="mwBNE">armel: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ARMv5" title="ARMv5" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBNI">ARMv5</a> 32-bit for use on legacy embedded systems<sup about="#mwt584" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-128" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-128&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-128" id="mwBNM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBNQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBNU">[</span>128<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBNY">]</span></span></a></sup> (support dropped from <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt580" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBNc" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;unstable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt580" id="mwBNg">unstable</span> on 2025-11-03<sup about="#mwt587" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-129" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-129&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-129" id="mwBNk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBNo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBNs">[</span>129<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBNw">]</span></span></a></sup>)</li>
<li id="mwBN0">armhf: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ARMv7" title="ARMv7" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBN4">ARMv7</a> 32-bit, requires a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Floating-point_unit" title="Floating-point unit" id="mwBN8">floating-point unit</a></li>
<li id="mwBOA">ppc64el: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PowerPC" title="PowerPC" id="mwBOE">PowerPC</a> 64-bit for use with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/POWER7" title="POWER7" id="mwBOI">POWER7</a>+ and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/POWER8" title="POWER8" id="mwBOM">POWER8</a> CPUs</li>
<li id="mwBOQ">riscv64: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RISC-V" title="RISC-V" id="mwBOU">RISC-V</a> 64-bit</li>
<li id="mwBOY">s390x: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Z/Architecture" title="Z/Architecture" id="mwBOc">z/Architecture</a> 64-bit<sup about="#mwt588" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-trixie-supported-architectures_5-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;trixie-supported-architectures&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-trixie-supported-architectures-5" id="mwBOg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBOk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBOo">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBOs">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

<p id="mwBOw">Unofficial ports are available as part of the <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt589" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBO0" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Mono/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mono&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Mono&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;unstable&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt589" id="mwBO4">unstable</span> distribution:</p>
<ul id="mwBO8"><li id="mwBPA">alpha: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DEC_Alpha" title="DEC Alpha" id="mwBPE">DEC Alpha</a></li>
<li id="mwBPI">hppa: HP <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PA-RISC" title="PA-RISC" id="mwBPM">PA-RISC</a></li>
<li id="mwBPQ">hurd-i386: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GNU_Hurd" title="GNU Hurd" id="mwBPU">GNU Hurd</a> kernel on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IA-32" title="IA-32" id="mwBPY">IA-32</a></li>
<li id="mwBPc">hurd-amd64: GNU Hurd kernel on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X86-64" title="X86-64" id="mwBPg">x86-64</a></li>
<li id="mwBPk">i386: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IA-32" title="IA-32" id="mwBPo">IA-32</a> 32-bit, compatible with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X86" title="X86" id="mwBPs">x86</a> machines<sup about="#mwt591" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-supported-hardware_124-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;supported-hardware&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-supported-hardware-124" id="mwBPw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBP0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBP4">[</span>124<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBP8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBQA">loong64: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loongson#LoongArch" title="Loongson" id="mwBQE">LoongArch</a><sup about="#mwt594" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-130" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-130&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-130" id="mwBQI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBQM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBQQ">[</span>130<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBQU">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBQY">mips64el: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MIPS_architecture" title="MIPS architecture" id="mwBQc">MIPS</a> 64-bit</li>
<li id="mwBQg">m68k: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Motorola_68000_series" title="Motorola 68000 series" id="mwBQk">Motorola 68k</a> on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amiga" title="Amiga" id="mwBQo">Amiga</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atari_ST" title="Atari ST" id="mwBQs">Atari</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mac_(computer)" title="Mac (computer)" id="mwBQw">Macintosh</a> and various embedded <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/VMEbus" title="VMEbus" id="mwBQ0">VME</a> systems</li>
<li id="mwBQ4">powerpc: PowerPC 32-bit</li>
<li id="mwBQ8">sh4: Hitachi <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SuperH" title="SuperH" id="mwBRA">SuperH</a></li>
<li id="mwBRE">sparc64: Sun <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SPARC" title="SPARC" id="mwBRI">SPARC</a> 64-bit</li>
<li id="mwBRM">x32: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X32_ABI" title="X32 ABI" id="mwBRQ">x32 ABI</a> for x86-64<sup about="#mwt597" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-131" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-131&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-131" id="mwBRU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBRY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRc">[</span>131<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRg">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

<p id="mwBRk">Debian supports a variety of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ARM_architecture" title="ARM architecture" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBRo">ARM</a>-based <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Network-attached_storage" title="Network-attached storage" id="mwBRs">network-attached storage</a> (NAS) devices. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NSLU2" title="NSLU2" id="mwBRw">NSLU2</a> was supported by the installer in Debian 4.0 and 5.0,<sup about="#mwt600" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-132" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-132&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-132" id="mwBR0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBR4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBR8">[</span>132<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBSA">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martin_Michlmayr" title="Martin Michlmayr" id="mwBSE">Martin Michlmayr</a> is providing installation <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tar_(computing)" title="Tar (computing)" id="mwBSI">tarballs</a> since version 6.0.<sup about="#mwt603" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-133" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-133&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-133" id="mwBSM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBSQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBSU">[</span>133<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBSY">]</span></span></a></sup> Other supported NAS devices are the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buffalo_network-attached_storage_series" title="Buffalo network-attached storage series" id="mwBSc">Buffalo</a> Kurobox Pro, GLAN Tank, Thecus N2100<sup about="#mwt606" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-134" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-134&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-134" id="mwBSg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBSk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBSo">[</span>134<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBSs">]</span></span></a></sup> and QNAP Turbo Stations.<sup about="#mwt609" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-135" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-135&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-135" id="mwBSw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBS0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBS4">[</span>135<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBS8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBTA">Devices based on the Kirkwood <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/System_on_a_chip" title="System on a chip" id="mwBTE">system on a chip</a> (SoC) are supported too, such as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SheevaPlug" title="SheevaPlug" id="mwBTI">SheevaPlug</a> plug computer and OpenRD products.<sup about="#mwt612" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-136" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-136&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-136" id="mwBTM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBTQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBTU">[</span>136<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBTY">]</span></span></a></sup> There are efforts to run Debian on mobile devices, but this is not a project goal yet since the Debian Linux kernel maintainers would not apply the needed patches.<sup about="#mwt615" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-137" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-137&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-137" id="mwBTc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBTg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBTk">[</span>137<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBTo">]</span></span></a></sup> Nevertheless, packages exist for resource-limited systems.<sup about="#mwt618" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-138" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-138&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-138" id="mwBTs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBTw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBT0">[</span>138<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBT4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBT8">There are efforts to support Debian on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wireless_access_point" title="Wireless access point" id="mwBUA">wireless access points</a>.<sup about="#mwt621" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-139" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-139&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-139" id="mwBUE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBUI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUM">[</span>139<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Debian is known to run on set-top boxes.<sup about="#mwt624" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-140" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-140&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-140" id="mwBUU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBUY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUc">[</span>140<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUg">]</span></span></a></sup> Work is ongoing to support the AM335x processor,<sup about="#mwt627" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-141" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-141&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-141" id="mwBUk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBUo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUs">[</span>141<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUw">]</span></span></a></sup> which is used in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Point_of_sale" title="Point of sale" id="mwBU0">electronic point of service</a> solutions.<sup about="#mwt630" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-142" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-142&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-142" id="mwBU4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBU8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBVA">[</span>142<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBVE">]</span></span></a></sup> Debian may be customized to run on cash machines.<sup about="#mwt633" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-143" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-143&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-143" id="mwBVI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBVM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBVQ">[</span>143<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBVU">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BeagleBoard" title="BeagleBoard" id="mwBVY">BeagleBoard</a>, a low-power <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Open-source_hardware" title="Open-source hardware" id="mwBVc">open-source hardware</a> single-board computer made by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texas_Instruments" title="Texas Instruments" id="mwBVg">Texas Instruments</a>, has switched to Debian Linux preloaded on its Beaglebone Black board's flash. Roqos Core, a x86-64 based IPS firewall router, runs on Debian Linux.</p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="47" id="mwBVk" aria-labelledby="Organization"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Organization">Organization</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Debian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=47" title="Edit section: Organization"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<div class="thumb floatright" style="" about="#mwt634" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBVo" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Image frame\n&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Image_frame&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;content&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{tree chart/start}}\n{{tree chart| | | | | |GR |GR=General Resolution}}\n{{tree chart|el |ov |Q|Q|el=elect↓|ov=override↓|boxstyle_el=border: 0; text-align: left;|boxstyle_ov=border: 0; text-align: right;}}\n{{tree chart|S|DPL |P|P|G|Q|DPL=Leader}}\n{{tree chart|Q| |Q|app |Q|Q|app=↓appoint|boxstyle_app=border: 0; text-align: left;}}\n{{tree chart|Q|DEL |P|P|Z|Q|DEL=Delegate}}\n{{tree chart|Q| |Q|dec | |Q|dec=↓decide|boxstyle_dec=border: 0; text-align: left;}}\n{{tree chart|Y|DD |pr |Q|DD=Developer|pr=propose↑|boxstyle_pr=border: 0; text-align: right;}}\n{{tree chart| | |Y|P|P|P|P|Z}}\n{{tree chart/end}}&quot;},&quot;caption&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Simplified organizational structure&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><div class="thumbinner" style="width: fit-content;"><div class="thumbimage noresize" style="width: auto; ">
